            "id" -> "1908.08030", "submitter" -> "Davide Fioravanti", 
             "authors" -> "Davide Fioravanti, Daniele Gregori", "title" -> 
             "Integrability and cycles of deformed ${\\cal N}=2$ gauge \
theory", "comments" -> "15 pages, Latex", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/j.physletb.2020.135376", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  To analyse pure ${\\cal N}=2$ $SU(2)$ gauge theory in the \
Nekrasov-Shatashvili\n(NS) limit (or deformed Seiberg-Witten (SW)), we use \
the Ordinary Differential\nEquation/Integrable Model (ODE/IM) correspondence, \
and in particular its\n(broken) discrete symmetry in its extended version \
with {\\it two} singular\nirregular points. Actually, this symmetry appears \
to be 'manifestation' of the\nspontaneously broken $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ R-symmetry \
of the original gauge problem\nand the two deformed SW cycles are simply \
connected to the Baxter's $T$ and $Q$\nfunctions, respectively, of the \
Liouville conformal field theory at the\nself-dual point. The liaison is \
realised via a second order differential\noperator which is essentially the \
'quantum' version of the square of the SW\ndifferential. Moreover, the \
constraints imposed by the broken $\\mathbb{Z}_2$\nR-symmetry acting on the \
moduli space (Bilal-Ferrari equations) seem to have\ntheir quantum \
counterpart in the $TQ$ and the $T$ periodicity relations, and\nintegrability \
yields also a useful Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) for the\ncycles \
($Y(\\theta,\\pm u)$ or their square roots, $Q(\\theta,\\pm u)$). A latere,\n\
two efficient asymptotic expansion techniques are presented. Clearly, the \
whole\nconstruction is extendable to gauge theories with matter and/or higher \
rank\ngroups.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 21 Aug 2019 17:52:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2020-03-25", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fioravanti", "Davide", ""}, {
