            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study in detail the Schr\\\"{o}dinger equation \
corresponding to the four\ndimensional $SU(2)$ $\\mathcal{N}=2$ SQCD theory \
with one flavour. We calculate\nthe Voros symbols, or quantum periods, in \
four different ways: Borel summation\nof the WKB series, direct computation \
of Wronskians of exponentially decaying\nsolutions, the TBA equations of \
Gaiotto-Moore-Neitzke/Gaiotto, and instanton\ncounting. We make computations \
by all of these methods, finding good agreement.\nWe also study the exact \
quantization condition for the spectrum, and we compute\nthe Fredholm \
determinant of the inverse of the Schr\\\"odinger operator using the\nTS/ST \
correspondence and Zamolodchikov's TBA, again finding good agreement. In\n\
addition, we explore two aspects of the relationship between singularities of\
\nthe Borel transformed WKB series and BPS states: BPS states of the 4d \
theory\nare related to singularities in the Borel transformed WKB series for \
the\nquantum periods, and BPS states of a coupled 2d+4d system are related to\
\nsingularities in the Borel transformed WKB series for local solutions of \
the\nSchr\\\"odinger equation.\n", 
