            "categories" -> "hep-th astro-ph.HE gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  QNMs govern the linear response to perturbations of BHs, \
D-branes and\nfuzzballs and the gravitational wave signals in the ring-down \
phase of binary\nmergers. A remarkable connection between QNMs of neutral BHs \
in 4d and quantum\nSW geometries describing the dynamics of ${\\cal N}=2$ SYM \
theories has been\nrecently put forward. We extend the gauge/gravity \
dictionary to a large class\nof gravity backgrounds including charged and \
rotating BHs of Einstein-Maxwell\ntheory in $d=4,5$ dimensions, D3-branes, \
D1D5 `circular' fuzzballs and smooth\nhorizonless geometries; all related to \
${\\cal N}=2$ SYM with a single $SU(2)$\ngauge group and fundamental matter. \
We find that photon-spheres, a common\nfeature of all examples, are \
associated to degenerations of the classical\nelliptic SW geometry whereby a \
cycle pinches to zero size. Quantum effects\nresolve the singular geometry \
and lead to a spectrum of quantized energies,\nlabeled by the overtone number \
$n$. We compute the spectrum of QNMs using exact\nWKB quantization, geodetic \
motion and numerical simulations and show excellent\nagreement between the \
three methods. We explicitly illustrate our findings for\nthe case D3-brane \
QNMs.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 10 May 2021 10:19:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 21 Jun 2021 15:19:54 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
