            "  If we start from certain functional relations as definition of \
a quantum\nintegrable theory, then we can derive from them a linear integral \
equation. It\ncan be extended, by introducing dynamical variables, to become \
an equation with\nthe form of Marchenko's. Then, we derive from the latter a \
classical\n(differential) Lax pair. We exemplify our method by focusing on \
the massive\nversion of the ODE/IM (Ordinary Differential \
Equations/Integrable Models)\ncorrespondence from Quantum sine-Gordon (sG) \
with many moduli/masses to the\nclassical sinh-Gordon (shG) equation, so \
