             "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc nlin.SI", "license" -> 
             "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
             "  We develop a new method for writing simple exact equations \
characterizing\ngravity solutions among which black holes and in particular \
the quasinormal\nmodes. More precisely, we derive the full system of \
functional and\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz non linear integral equations of \
quantum\nintegrability. In particular, we prove that the Quasinormal Modes \
verify\ndifferent equivalent exact quantization conditions and identify them \
with Bethe\nroots. We numerically solve the integral equation and compare the \
results with\nother methods. Eventually, we can definitely certify its \
simplicity, accuracy\nand effectiveness. Furthermore, this method connects \
different unexpected\nfields and paves the way for innovative ways of \
investigations in gravity and\ngauge theories.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
