            "TBA-like equations for non-planar scattering amplitude/Wilson \
lines\n  duality at strong coupling", "comments" -> "31 pages, 8 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2022)099", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the minimal area of a string worldsheet ending on \
two infinite\nperiodic light-like Wilson lines in the AdS$_3$ boundary, which \
is dual to the\nfirst non-planar correction to the gluon scattering amplitude \
in\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM at the strong coupling. Using the connection between \
the\nHitchin system and the thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) equations, we \
present\nan analytic method to compute the minimal area surface and express \
the\nnon-trivial part of the minimal area in terms of the free energy of the\n\
TBA-like equations. Given the cross ratios as inputs, the area computed from\n\
the TBA-like equations matches that calculated using the numerical \
integration.\n", 
