            "  We study the WKB analysis of the solutions to the linear \
problem for a\nmodified affine Toda field equation, which is equivalent to \
the higher-order\nordinary differential equation (ODE) studied in the ODE/IM \
correspondence.\nAfter gauge transformation, we diagonalize the flat \
connection of the linear\nproblem to reduce the latter to a set of \
independent first-order linear\ndifferential equations. We explicitly perform \
this procedure for classical\naffine Lie algebras with lower ranks. In \
particular, we study the WKB solutions\nof the $D_r^{(1)}$- and \
$D^{(2)}_{r+1}$-type linear problems, which correspond\nto the higher-order \
ODEs with the pseudo-differential operator. The\ndiagonalized connection is \
obtained from the Riccati equations of the adjoint\nlinear problem and \
related to the conserved currents of the integrable\nhierarchy constructed by \
Drinfeld and Sokolov up to total derivatives.\n", 
