               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andrea Cipriani, Carlo Di Benedetto, Giorgio Di Russo, \
Alfredo Grillo,\\n  Giuseppe Sudano\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Charge (in)stability and superradiance of Topological \
Stars\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"32 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study linear massive scalar charged perturbations of \
Topological Stars in\\nthe fuzzball and in the black hole (Black String) \
regimes. The objects that\\nnaturally couple to the electric 3-form field \
strength of these solutions are\\ncharged strings, wound around the compact \
direction. We explore the possibility\\nof instabilities of these solutions, \
in analogy with the charge instability\\nalready highlighted for other \
non-BPS geometries like JMaRT. This issue is\\naddressed by calculating \
quasi-normal mode frequencies with a variety of\\ntechniques: WKB \
approximation, direct integration, Leaver method and by\\nexploiting the \
recently discovered correspondence between black hole-fuzzball\\nperturbation \
theory and quantum Seiberg-Witten curves. All mode frequencies we\\nfind have \
negative imaginary parts, implying an exponential decay in time. \
This\\nsuggests a linear stability of Topological Stars also in this new \
scenario. In\\naddition, we study the charge superradiance for the Black \
String. We compute\\nthe amplification factor with the numerical integration \
method and a quantum\\nSeiberg-Witten motivated definition including \
instantonic corrections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
