            "  We study linear massive scalar charged perturbations of \
Topological Stars in\nthe fuzzball and in the black hole (Black String) \
regimes. The objects that\nnaturally couple to the electric 3-form field \
strength of these solutions are\ncharged strings, wound around the compact \
direction. We explore the possibility\nof instabilities of these solutions, \
in analogy with the charge instability\nalready highlighted for other non-BPS \
geometries like JMaRT. This issue is\naddressed by calculating quasi-normal \
mode frequencies with a variety of\ntechniques: WKB approximation, direct \
integration, Leaver method and by\nexploiting the recently discovered \
