                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct TBA equations for D-type Argyres-Douglas \
theories with an SU(2)\\nflavor symmetry based on their spectral networks. We \
show that the solutions of\\nthese TBA equations agree with the quantum \
periods of the corresponding quantum\\nSeiberg-Witten curves defined in the \
Nekrosov-Shatashvili limit of the Omega\\nbackground, including a centrifugal \
correction. We study the variety of TBA\\nsystems across the Coulomb branch \
moduli space and find that they correspond to\\nthe Dynkin diagrams of $D_n$ \
Lie algebras in the minimal chamber, and reproduce\\nthe TBA equations for \
reflectionless D scattering theories at the maximally\\nsymmetric point. \
Numerical computations demonstrate that the quantum periods\\nobtained from \
the Borel-Pad\\\\'e resummation and their WKB expansions are in\\nagreement \
with the solutions of the TBA equations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
