 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Connection formulas relating Frobenius solutions of \
linear ODEs at different\\nFuchsian singular points can be expressed in terms \
of the large order\\nasymptotics of the corresponding power series. We \
demonstrate that for the\\nusual, confluent and reduced confluent Heun \
equation, the series expansion of\\nthe relevant asymptotic amplitude in a \
suitable parameter can be systematically\\ncomputed to arbitrary order. This \
allows to check a recent conjecture of\\nBonelli-Iossa-Panea Lichtig-Tanzini \
expressing the Heun connection matrix in\\nterms of quasiclassical Virasoro \
conformal blocks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
