            "title" -> "Freedom near Lightcone and ANEC Saturation", 
            "comments" -> "38 pages. v3: Minor changes, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2023)065", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Averaged Null Energy Conditions (ANECs) hold in unitary \
quantum field\ntheories. In conformal field theories, ANECs in states created \
by the\napplication of the stress tensor to the vacuum lead to three \
constraints on the\nstress-tensor three-point couplings, depending on the \
choice of polarization.\nThe same constraints follow from considering \
two-point functions of the stress\ntensor in a thermal state and focusing on \
the contribution of the stress tensor\nin the operator product expansion \
(OPE). One can observe this in holographic\nGauss-Bonnet gravity, where ANEC \
saturation coincides with the appearance of\nsuperluminal signal propagation \
in thermal states. We show that, when this\nhappens, the corresponding \
generalizations of ANECs for higher-spin\nmulti-stress tensor operators with \
minimal twist are saturated as well and all\ncontributions from such \
operators to the thermal two-point functions vanish in\nthe lightcone limit. \
This leads to a special near-lightcone behavior of the\nthermal stress-tensor \
correlators -- they take the vacuum form, independent of\ntemperature.\n", 
