                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the problem of analytically computing the \
one point functions for\\nscalar fields in planar AdS black holes of \
arbitrary dimension, which are\\nsourced by the Weyl squared tensor. We \
analyze the problem in terms of power\\nseries expansions around the boundary \
using the method of Frobenius. We clarify\\nthe pole structure of the final \
answer in terms of operator mixing, as argued\\npreviously by Grinberg and \
Maldacena. We generalize the techniques to also\\nobtain analytic results for \
slowly modulated spatially varying sources to first\\nnon-trivial order in \
the wave vector for arbitrary dimension. We also study the\\nfirst order \
corrections to the one point function of the global AdS black hole\\nat large \
mass, where we perturb in terms that correspond to the curvature of\\nthe \
horizon.\\n\""}]}, {
