         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2211.05144", "submitter" -> "David Berenstein", "authors" -> 
            "David Berenstein, Robinson Mancilla", "title" -> 
            "Aspects of thermal one-point functions and response functions in \
AdS\n  Black holes", "comments" -> "v2: references added, minor typos fixed", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.107.126010", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the problem of analytically computing the one point \
functions for\nscalar fields in planar AdS black holes of arbitrary \
dimension, which are\nsourced by the Weyl squared tensor. We analyze the \
problem in terms of power\nseries expansions around the boundary using the \
method of Frobenius. We clarify\nthe pole structure of the final answer in \
terms of operator mixing, as argued\npreviously by Grinberg and Maldacena. We \
generalize the techniques to also\nobtain analytic results for slowly \
modulated spatially varying sources to first\nnon-trivial order in the wave \
vector for arbitrary dimension. We also study the\nfirst order corrections to \
the one point function of the global AdS black hole\nat large mass, where we \
perturb in terms that correspond to the curvature of\nthe horizon.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
