 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note we present some results on the convergence \
of Nekrasov partition\\nfunctions as power series in the instanton counting \
parameter. We focus on\\n$U(N)$ ${\\\\mathcal N}=2$ gauge theories in four \
dimensions with matter in the\\nadjoint and in the fundamental \
representations of the gauge group respectively\\nand find rigorous lower \
bounds for the convergence radius in the two cases: if\\nthe theory is \
{\\\\it conformal}, then the series has at least a {\\\\it finite}\\nradius \
of convergence, while if it is {\\\\it asymptotically free} it has \
{\\\\it\\ninfinite} radius of convergence. Via AGT correspondence, this \
implies that the\\nrelated irregular conformal blocks of $W_N$ algebrae admit \
a power expansion in\\nthe modulus converging in the whole plane. By \
specifying to the $SU(2)$ case,\\nwe apply our results to analyse the \
convergence properties of the corresponding\\nPainlev\\\\'e \
$\\\\tau$-functions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
