               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  By exploiting the Kerr-Schild gauge, we study the \
scattering of a massive\\n(charged) scalar off a Kerr-Newman black hole. In \
this gauge, the interactions\\nbetween the probe and the target involve only \
tri-linear vertices. We manage to\\nwrite down the tree-level scattering \
amplitudes in analytic form, from which we\\ncan construct an expression for \
the eikonal phase which is exact in the spin of\\nthe black hole at arbitrary \
order in the Post-Minkowskian expansion. We compute\\nthe classical \
contribution to the cross-section and deflection angle at leading\\norder for \
a Kerr black hole for arbitrary orientation of the spin. Finally, we\\ntest \
our method by reproducing the classical amplitude for a Schwarzschild\\nblack \
hole at second Post-Minkowskian order and outline how to extend \
the\\nanalysis to the Kerr-Newman case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
