          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2307.14616\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jiliang Jing\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Changkai Chen and Jiliang Jing\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Radiation fluxes of gravitational, electromagnetic, and \
scalar\\n  perturbations in type-D black holes: an exact approach\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"23 pages, 5 figures, and 6 tables\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JCAP 11 (2023) 070\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a novel method that solves Teukolsky \
equations with the source to\\ncalculate radiation fluxes at infinity and \
event horizon for any perturbation\\nfields of type-D black holes. For the \
first time, we use the confluent Heun\\nfunction to obtain the exact \
solutions of ingoing and outgoing waves for the\\nTeukolsky equation. This \
benefits from our derivation of the asymptotic\\nanalytic expression of the \
confluent Heun function at infinity. It is\\ninteresting to note that these \
exact solutions are not subject to any\\nconstraints, such as low-frequency \
and weak-field. To illustrate the\\ncorrectness, we apply these exact \
solutions to calculate the gravitational,\\nelectromagnetic, and scalar \
radiations of the Schwarzschild black hole.\\nNumerical results show that the \
proposed exact solution appreciably improves\\nthe computational accuracy and \
efficiency compared with the 23rd post-Newtonian\\norder expansion and the \
Mano-Suzuki-Takasugi method.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
