           "id" -> "2307.14616", "submitter" -> "Jiliang Jing", "authors" -> 
            "Changkai Chen and Jiliang Jing", "title" -> 
            "Radiation fluxes of gravitational, electromagnetic, and scalar\n \
 perturbations in type-D black holes: an exact approach", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 5 figures, and 6 tables", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JCAP 11 (2023) 070", "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a novel method that solves Teukolsky equations with \
the source to\ncalculate radiation fluxes at infinity and event horizon for \
any perturbation\nfields of type-D black holes. For the first time, we use \
the confluent Heun\nfunction to obtain the exact solutions of ingoing and \
outgoing waves for the\nTeukolsky equation. This benefits from our derivation \
of the asymptotic\nanalytic expression of the confluent Heun function at \
infinity. It is\ninteresting to note that these exact solutions are not \
subject to any\nconstraints, such as low-frequency and weak-field. To \
illustrate the\ncorrectness, we apply these exact solutions to calculate the \
gravitational,\nelectromagnetic, and scalar radiations of the Schwarzschild \
black hole.\nNumerical results show that the proposed exact solution \
appreciably improves\nthe computational accuracy and efficiency compared with \
the 23rd post-Newtonian\norder expansion and the Mano-Suzuki-Takasugi method.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
