          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2307.14847\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Srijan Kumar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David, Srijan Kumar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermal one-point functions: CFT's with fermions, large \
$d$ and large\\n  spin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"46 pages, 8 figures, some more typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We apply the OPE inversion formula on thermal two-point \
functions of fermions\\nto obtain thermal one-point function of fermion \
bi-linears appearing in the\\ncorresponding OPE. We primarily focus on the \
OPE channel which contains the\\nstress tensor of the theory. We apply our \
formalism to the mean field theory of\\nfermions and verify that the \
inversion formula reproduces the spectrum as well\\nas their corresponding \
thermal one-point functions. We then examine the large\\n$N$ critical \
Gross-Neveu model in $d=2k+1$ dimensions with $k$ even and at\\nfinite \
temperature. We show that stress tensor evaluated from the \
inversion\\nformula agrees with that evaluated from the partition function at \
the critical\\npoint. We demonstrate the expectation values of 3 different \
classes of higher\\nspin currents are all related to each other by numerical \
constants, spin and\\nthe thermal mass. We evaluate the ratio of the thermal \
expectation values of\\nhigher spin currents at the critical point to the \
Gaussian fixed point or the\\nStefan-Boltzmann result, both for the large $N$ \
critical $O(N)$ model and the\\nGross-Neveu model in odd dimensions. This \
ratio is always less than one and it\\napproaches unity on increasing the \
spin with the dimension $d$ held fixed. The\\nratio however approaches zero \
when the dimension $d$ is increased with the spin\\nheld fixed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 27 Jul 2023 13:24:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 21 Aug 2023 12:27:42 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 23 Oct 2023 13:46:40 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-10-24\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"David\"", ",", "\"Justin R.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kumar\"", ",", "\"Srijan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
