          DiskBox[{2.8802516458746013`, 4.995668714600318}, 
           0.06364453000660265],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2308.01371\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timotej Lemut\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sa\\\\v{s}o Grozdanov, Timotej Lemut, Juan F. \
Pedraza\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Reconstruction of the quasinormal spectrum from \
pole-skipping\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 108, L101901 (2023)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.108.L101901\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IFT-UAM/CSIC-23-94\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The holographic gauge/gravity duality provides an \
explicit reduction of\\nquantum field theory (QFT) calculations in the \
semi-classical large-$N$ limit\\nto sets of `gravitational' differential \
equations whose analysis can reveal all\\ndetails of the spectra of thermal \
QFT correlators. We argue that in certain\\ncases, a complete reconstruction \
of the spectrum and of the corresponding\\ncorrelator is possible from only \
the knowledge of an infinite, discrete set of\\npole-skipping points \
traversed by a single (hydrodynamic) mode computed in a\\nseries expansion in \
an inverse number of spacetime dimensions. Conceptually,\\nthis reduces the \
computation of a QFT correlator spectrum to performing a set\\nof purely \
algebraic manipulations. With the help of the pole-skipping analysis,\\nwe \
also uncover a novel structure underpinning the coefficients that enter \
the\\nhydrodynamic dispersion relations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 2 Aug 2023 18:24:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
