               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2308.03229\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kuo-Wei Huang\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kuo-Wei Huang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Toward Null State Equations in $d>2$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages, v2: minor corrections and references added, v3: \
notation\\n  improved\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP11(2023)203\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2023)203\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In two-dimensional CFTs with a large central charge, \
the level-two BPZ\\nequation governs the heavy-light scalar four-point \
correlator when the light\\nprobe scalar has dimension $h= - {1\\\\over 2}$; \
the corresponding linear ordinary\\ndifferential equation can be recast into \
a schematic form $x^2 u_{xx}+u=0$. In\\nthis paper, we make an observation \
that in a class of four-dimensional CFTs\\nwith a large central charge, the \
heavy-light scalar correlator in the\\nnear-lightcone limit obeys a similar \
equation, $x^3 u_{xxxy}+u=0$, when the\\nlight scalar has dimension \
$\\\\Delta=-1$. We focus on the multi-stress tensor\\nsector of the theory \
and also discuss the corresponding equations for the cases\\nwith $\\\\Delta \
= -2, -3$. The solutions to these linear partial differential\\nequations in \
higher dimensions are shown, after a suitable change of variables,\\nto \
reproduce the near-lightcone correlators previously obtained via \
holography\\nand the conformal bootstrap.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
