explicitly elucidated. The inclusion of\nthe scalar field imparts a \
non-constant Ricci curvature to the domain wall,\nthereby rendering these \
configurations particularly suitable for the\nconstruction of two-dimensional \
quantum black holes. To establish a well-posed\nvariational principle in the \
presence of the domain wall, two essential steps\nare undertaken. First, we \
extend the conventional renormalized AdS$_3$ action\nto accommodate the \
presence of the scalar field. Second, to establish a\nwell-posed variational \
principle, we extend the renormalized AdS$_3$ action to\ninclude the scalar \
field and incorporate the Gibbons--Hawking--York term for\ninternal \
boundaries and domain wall tension. We engage in holographic\ncomputations, \
thereby determining the explicit form of the holographic stress\ntensor. In \
this context, the stress tensor can be expressed as that of a\nperfect fluid \
situated on a curved background. Additionally, it paves the road\nto \
ascertain the spacetime mass. Finally, we close by demonstrating the\n\
existence of three-dimensional accelerating spacetimes with asymptotically\n\
locally flat and asymptotically locally de Sitter geometries, particularly\n\
those embodying black holes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 11 Sep 2023 15:47:40 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 13 Nov 2023 21:01:45 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
