                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study linear scalar perturbations of slowly \
accelerating\\nKerr-Newman-anti-de Sitter black holes using the method of \
isomonodromic\\ndeformations. The conformally coupled Klein-Gordon equation \
separates into two\\nsecond-order ordinary differential equations with five \
singularities.\\nNevertheless, the angular equation can be transformed into a \
Heun equation, for\\nwhich we provide an asymptotic expansion for the angular \
eigenvalues in the\\nsmall acceleration and rotation limit. In the radial \
case, we recast the\\nboundary value problem in terms of a set of initial \
conditions for the\\nisomonodromic tau function of Fuchsian systems with five \
regular singular\\npoints. For the sake of illustration, we compute the \
quasi-normal modes\\nfrequencies.\\n\""}]}, {
