            "Scalar quasi-normal modes of accelerating Kerr-Newman-AdS black \
holes", "comments" -> "22 pages, 5 figures, published in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 02 (2024) 189", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP02(2024)189", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study linear scalar perturbations of slowly accelerating\n\
Kerr-Newman-anti-de Sitter black holes using the method of isomonodromic\n\
deformations. The conformally coupled Klein-Gordon equation separates into \
two\nsecond-order ordinary differential equations with five singularities.\n\
Nevertheless, the angular equation can be transformed into a Heun equation, \
for\nwhich we provide an asymptotic expansion for the angular eigenvalues in \
the\nsmall acceleration and rotation limit. In the radial case, we recast the\
\nboundary value problem in terms of a set of initial conditions for the\n\
isomonodromic tau function of Fuchsian systems with five regular singular\n\
points. For the sake of illustration, we compute the quasi-normal modes\n\
frequencies.\n", 
