               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Matter falling into a Schwarzschild-AdS black hole from \
the left causes\\nincreased focussing of ingoing geodesics from the right, \
and, as a consequence,\\nthey reach the singularity sooner. In a standard \
Penrose diagram, the\\nsingularity \\\"bends down\\\". We show how to detect \
this feature of the singularity\\nholographically, using a boundary two-point \
function. We model the matter with\\na shock wave, and show that this bending \
down of the singularity can be read\\noff from a novel analytic continuation \
of the boundary two-point function.\\nAlong the way, we obtain a \
generalization of the recently proposed thermal\\nproduct formula for \
two-point correlators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
