            "title" -> 
            "Boundary signature of singularity in the presence of a shock \
wave", "comments" -> "55 pages, 9 figures; v2: added references", 
            "journal-ref" -> "SciPost Phys. 16, 060 (2024)", "doi" -> 
            "10.21468/SciPostPhys.16.2.060", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Matter falling into a Schwarzschild-AdS black hole from the \
left causes\nincreased focussing of ingoing geodesics from the right, and, as \
a consequence,\nthey reach the singularity sooner. In a standard Penrose \
diagram, the\nsingularity \"bends down\". We show how to detect this feature \
of the singularity\nholographically, using a boundary two-point function. We \
model the matter with\na shock wave, and show that this bending down of the \
singularity can be read\noff from a novel analytic continuation of the \
boundary two-point function.\nAlong the way, we obtain a generalization of \
the recently proposed thermal\nproduct formula for two-point correlators.\n", 
