                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive a gauge inspired combinatorial formula based \
on localization for\\nthe Post-Newtonian expansion of the gravitational wave \
form luminosity of\\nbinary systems made of objects with very different \
masses orbiting at large\\ndistances and small velocities. The results are \
tested against previous\\nformulae in the literature for Schwarschild and \
Kerr black holes at the 5th and\\n3rd Post Newtonian order respectively \
beyond the quadrupole approximation.\\nTidal effects show up in the wave form \
at the 5th PN order, providing a\\nquantitative measure of the \
blackness/compactness properties of the heavy\\nobject.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
