               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Changkai Chen, Jiliang Jing\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gravitational wave fluxes on generic orbits in \
near-extreme Kerr\\n  spacetime: higher spin and large eccentricity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages. Update: corrected errors in Eqs. (32-33)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sci. China-Phys. Mech. Astron. 67, 110411 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s11433-024-2431-0\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  To obtain the waveform template of gravitational waves \
(GWs), substantial\\ncomputational resources and exceedingly high precision \
are often required. In\\nthe previous study [JCAP 11 (2023) 070], we \
efficiently and accurately\\ncalculate GW fluxes of a particle in circular \
orbits around a Schwarzschild\\nblack hole using the confluent Heun function. \
We extend the previous method to\\ncalculate the asymptotic GW fluxes from a \
particle in generic orbits around a\\nnear-extreme Kerr black hole. \
Especially when dealing with the computational\\ndifficulties in large \
eccentricity $e=0.9$, higher spin $a=0.999$, higher\\nharmonic modes, and \
strong-field regions, our results are much better than the\\nresults of the \
numerical integration method based on the \
Mano-Suzuki-Takasugi\\nmethod.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
