               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the classical dynamics of spinning particles \
using scattering\\namplitudes and eikonal exponentiation. We show that \
observables are determined\\nby a simple algorithm. A wealth of complexity \
arises in perturbation theory as\\npositions, momenta and spins must be \
iteratively corrected at each order. Even\\nthough we restrict ourselves to \
one-loop computations at quadratic order in\\nspin, nevertheless we encounter \
and resolve a number of subtle effects.\\nFinally, we clarify the links \
between our work and various other eikonal\\napproaches to spinning \
observables.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
