               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lara Bohnenblust, Harald Ita, Manfred Kraus, Johannes \
Schlenk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gravitational Bremsstrahlung in Black-Hole Scattering \
at\\n  $\\\\mathcal{O}(G^3)$: Linear-in-Spin Effects\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"50 pages, 10 figures, ancillary files\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PSI-PR-23-47\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the far-field time-domain waveform of the \
gravitational waves\\nproduced in the scattering of two spinning massive \
objects. The results include\\nlinear-in-spin ($S$) couplings and first-order \
gravitational corrections\\n($G^3$), and are valid for encounters in the \
weak-field regime. Employing a\\nfield-theory framework based on the \
scattering of massive scalar and vector\\nparticles coupled to \
Einstein-Hilbert gravity, we derive results for leading\\nand the \
next-to-leading spectral waveforms. We provide analytic expressions for\\nthe \
required scattering data, which include trees, one-loop amplitudes \
and\\ntheir cuts. The expressions are extracted from numerical amplitude \
evaluations\\nwith the Caravel program, using analytic reconstruction \
techniques applied in\\nthe classical limit. We confirm a recent prediction \
for infrared physics of the\\nclassical observable, and observe the \
surprising appearance of a ultraviolet\\nsingularity, which drops out in the \
far-field waveform.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
