               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2401.00574\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Syo Kamata\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Syo Kamata\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact WKB analysis for ${\\\\cal PT}$ symmetric quantum \
mechanics: Study of\\n  the Ai-Bender-Sarkar conjecture\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, 13 figures, v2: typo and minor corrections, v3: \
typo and\\n  grammar corrections, references added, another example added in \
Sec. 3.1,\\n  structure slightly modified, v4: edit format is changed, minor \
revision, Sec\\n  VI A is modified, the conclusion is unchanged, accepted in \
PRD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 109, 085023 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.109.085023\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider exact WKB analysis to a ${\\\\cal PT}$ \
symmetric quantum mechanics\\ndefined by the potential, $V(x) = \\\\omega^2 \
x^2 + g x^2(i x)^{\\\\varepsilon=2}$\\nwith $\\\\omega \\\\in {\\\\mathbb \
R}_{\\\\ge 0}$, $g \\\\in {\\\\mathbb R} _{> 0}$. We in\\nparticular aim to \
verify a conjecture proposed by Ai-Bender-Sarkar (ABS), that\\npertains to a \
relation between $D$-dimensional ${\\\\cal PT}$-symmetric theories\\nand \
analytic continuation (AC) of Hermitian theories concerning the \
energy\\nspectrum or Euclidean partition function. For the purpose, we \
construct energy\\nquantization conditions by exact WKB analysis and write \
down their transseries\\nsolution by solving the conditions. By performing \
alien calculus to the energy\\nsolutions, we verify validity of the ABS \
conjecture and seek a possibility of\\nits alternative form by Borel \
resummation theory if it is violated. Our results\\nclaim that the validity \
of the ABS conjecture drastically changes depending on\\nwhether $\\\\omega > \
0$ or $\\\\omega = 0$: If ${\\\\omega}>0$, then the ABS conjecture\\nis \
violated when exceeding the semi-classical level of the \
first\\nnon-perturbative order, but its alternative form is constructable by \
Borel\\nresummation theory. The ${\\\\cal PT}$ and the AC energies are \
related to each\\nother by a one-parameter Stokes automorphism, and a median \
resummed form, which\\ncorresponds to a formal exact solution, of the AC \
energy (resp. ${\\\\cal PT}$\\nenergy) is directly obtained by acting Borel \
resummation to a transseries\\nsolution of the ${\\\\cal PT}$ energy (resp. \
AC energy). If $\\\\omega = 0$, then,\\nwith respect to the inverse energy \
level-expansion, not only\\nperturbative/non-perturbative structures of the \
${\\\\cal PT}$ and the AC energies\\nbut also their perturbative parts do not \
match with each other. These energies\\nare independent solutions, and no \
alternative form of the ABS conjecture can be\\nreformulated by Borel \
resummation theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
