            "TBA equations and exact WKB analysis in deformed supersymmetric \
quantum\n  mechanics", "comments" -> "31 pages, 1 figure; Published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP03(2024)122", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2024)122", "report-no" -> "TIT/HEP- 698", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the spectral problem in deformed supersymmetric \
quantum mechanics\nwith polynomial superpotential by using the exact WKB \
method and the TBA\nequations. We apply the ODE/IM correspondence to the Schr\
\\\"odinger equation\nwith an effective potential deformed by integrating out \
the fermions, which\nadmits a continuous deformation parameter. We find that \
the TBA equations are\ndescribed by the ${\\mathbb Z}_4$-extended ones. For \
cubic superpotential\ncorresponding to the symmetric double-well potential, \
the TBA system splits\ninto the two $D_3$-type TBA equations. We investigate \
in detail this example\nbased on the TBA equations and their analytic \
continuation as well as the\nmassless limit. We find that the energy spectrum \
obtained from the exact\nquantization condition is in good agreement with the \
diagonalization approach\nof the Hamiltonian.\n", 
