            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2401.12454\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ming Chen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ming Chen, Gabriele Tartaglino-Mazzucchelli, Yao-Zhong \
Zhang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Charged massless scalar fields in a charged $C$-metric \
black hole: Exact\\n  solutions, Hawking radiation and scattering of scalar \
waves\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"33 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"gr-qc hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study Hawking radiation and wave scattering of \
charged scalar fields in a\\ncharged $C$-metric black hole background. The \
conformally invariant wave\\nequation for charged scalar fields can be \
separated into radial and angular\\nparts, each with five singularities. We \
show that the radial and angular\\nequations can be respectively transformed \
into the general Heun equation. We\\nexplore exact solutions of the radial \
Heun equation in terms of the local Heun\\nfunctions and connection \
coefficients. Exact behaviours of the asymptotic wave\\nfunctions are \
determined without approximations. We apply the exact results to\\nderive \
Hawking radiation, quasi-normal modes and superradiance. Since\\nquasinormal \
modes are significant for black holes through gravitional waves, we\\npresent \
the numeric results for quasinormal modes, and show the dependence upon\\nthe \
$C$-metric parameters and the charge of scalar fields. The \
analytic\\nexpressions of the solutions allow us to make fast numerical \
calculations of\\nhigh precision without restrictions on the model \
parameters.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
