            "title" -> 
            "Charged massless scalar fields in a charged $C$-metric black \
hole: Exact\n  solutions, Hawking radiation and scattering of scalar waves", 
            "comments" -> "33 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "gr-qc hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study Hawking radiation and wave scattering of charged \
scalar fields in a\ncharged $C$-metric black hole background. The conformally \
invariant wave\nequation for charged scalar fields can be separated into \
radial and angular\nparts, each with five singularities. We show that the \
radial and angular\nequations can be respectively transformed into the \
general Heun equation. We\nexplore exact solutions of the radial Heun \
equation in terms of the local Heun\nfunctions and connection coefficients. \
Exact behaviours of the asymptotic wave\nfunctions are determined without \
approximations. We apply the exact results to\nderive Hawking radiation, \
quasi-normal modes and superradiance. Since\nquasinormal modes are \
significant for black holes through gravitional waves, we\npresent the \
numeric results for quasinormal modes, and show the dependence upon\nthe \
$C$-metric parameters and the charge of scalar fields. The analytic\n\
expressions of the solutions allow us to make fast numerical calculations of\n\
high precision without restrictions on the model parameters.\n", 
