          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2404.06544\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mudit Rai\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mudit Rai and Luca Santoni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ladder Symmetries and Love Numbers of Reissner--Nordstr\\\
\\\\\"om Black Holes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2024)098\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is well known that asymptotically flat black holes \
in general relativity\\nhave vanishing tidal Love numbers. In the case of \
Schwarzschild and Kerr black\\nholes, this property has been shown to be a \
consequence of a hidden structure\\nof ladder symmetries for the \
perturbations. In this work, we extend the ladder\\nsymmetries to \
non-rotating charged black holes in general relativity. As\\nopposed to \
previous works in this context, we adopt a more general definition\\nof Love \
numbers, including quadratic operators that mix gravitational \
and\\nelectromagnetic perturbations in the point-particle effective field \
theory. We\\nshow that the calculation of a subset of those couplings in full \
general\\nrelativity is affected by an ambiguity in the split between source \
and\\nresponse, which we resolve through an analytic continuation. As a \
result, we\\nderive a novel master equation that unifies scalar, \
electromagnetic and\\ngravitational perturbations around \
Reissner--Nordstr\\\\\\\"om black holes. The\\nequation is hypergeometric and \
can be obtained from previous formulations via\\nnontrivial field \
redefinitions, which allow to systematically remove some of\\nthe \
singularities and make the presence of the ladder symmetries more \
manifest.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 9 Apr 2024 18:00:30 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
