            "  We study the binary dynamics of two Kerr black holes with \
arbitrary spin\nvectors in the presence of parity-even and parity-odd cubic \
deformations of\ngravity. We first derive the tree-level Compton amplitudes \
for a Kerr black\nhole in cubic gravity, which we then use to compute the \
two-to-two amplitudes\nof the massive bodies to leading order in the \
deformation and the\npost-Minkowskian expansion. The required one-loop \
computations are performed\nusing the leading singularity approach as well as \
the heavy-mass effective\nfield theory (HEFT) approach. These amplitudes are \
then used to compute the\nleading-order momentum and spin kick in cubic \
gravity in the KMOC formalism.\nOur results are valid for generic masses and \
spin vectors, and include all the\nindependent parity-even and parity-odd \
cubic deformations of Einstein-Hilbert\ngravity. We also present \
spin-expanded expressions for the momentum and spin\nkicks, and the all-order \
in spin deflection angle in the case of aligned spins.\n", 
