               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2406.00666\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shuta Ishigaki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shuta Ishigaki, Zhaojie Xu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermodynamics, magnetic properties, and global $U(1)$ \
symmetry breaking\\n  of the S-type Gubser-Rocha model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"23pages, 7 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study an explicit formula for the thermodynamic \
potential of the AdS\\ndyonic black brane solution with an axio-dilaton hair, \
which was discovered in\\nan extension of the $(3+1)$d Gubser-Rocha model \
enjoying S-duality. From the\\nthermodynamic potential, we can compute the \
magnetization and the magnetic\\nsusceptibilities of the dyonic solution. The \
result of the magnetization is\\nnegative implying that the system is \
diamagnetic. Subsequently, we consider a\\nspecific neutral limit of the \
dyonic solution. In this setup, we find that the\\nsystem exhibits \
spontaneous breaking of a global $U(1)$ symmetry. The order\\nparameter is \
given by a complex operator which is dual to the axio-dilaton\\nfield in the \
bulk. Interestingly, the system has a finite Hall conductivity\\neven in the \
absence of the external magnetic field, and it is related to the\\nphase of \
the complex operator.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 2 Jun 2024 08:29:05 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
