            "Shuta Ishigaki, Zhaojie Xu", "title" -> 
            "Thermodynamics, magnetic properties, and global $U(1)$ symmetry \
breaking\n  of the S-type Gubser-Rocha model", "comments" -> 
            "23pages, 7 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.str-el gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study an explicit formula for the thermodynamic potential \
of the AdS\ndyonic black brane solution with an axio-dilaton hair, which was \
discovered in\nan extension of the $(3+1)$d Gubser-Rocha model enjoying \
S-duality. From the\nthermodynamic potential, we can compute the \
magnetization and the magnetic\nsusceptibilities of the dyonic solution. The \
result of the magnetization is\nnegative implying that the system is \
diamagnetic. Subsequently, we consider a\nspecific neutral limit of the \
dyonic solution. In this setup, we find that the\nsystem exhibits spontaneous \
breaking of a global $U(1)$ symmetry. The order\nparameter is given by a \
complex operator which is dual to the axio-dilaton\nfield in the bulk. \
Interestingly, the system has a finite Hall conductivity\neven in the absence \
of the external magnetic field, and it is related to the\nphase of the \
complex operator.\n", 
