                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the covariant proposal for the \
gravitational Compton amplitude\\nfor a Kerr black hole. Employing the \
covariant three- and four-point Compton\\namplitudes, we assemble the \
classical one-loop integrand on the maximal cut at\\nall orders in spin, \
utilizing the method of unitarity. Expanding in powers of\\nspin, we evaluate \
the one-loop amplitude up to $\\\\mathcal O(G^2 a^8)$.\\nSupplemented with \
extra contact contributions derived from the far-zone data of\\nthe Teukolsky \
solutions, the one-loop amplitude is in agreement with results\\navailable in \
the literature. We showcase the classical eikonal in the\\naligned-spin case \
at $\\\\mathcal O(G^2 a^7)$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
