            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2407.08307\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ratna Koley\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Soham Chatterjee, Sagnik Roy and Ratna Koley\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Characterizing a class of accelerating wormholes with \
periodic potential\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The newly discovered Wormhole C--metric is a solution \
of Einstein's field\\nequation coupled with a phantom scalar field which \
describes the accelerated\\nwormholes. In the zero acceleration limit the \
solution reduces to an\\nasymptotically flat wormhole. For certain range of \
parameter space this\\nsolution doesn't possess any horizon, thus making it a \
viable candidate of\\nwormhole. To completely unveil this property we have \
studied the topological\\nproperties of this spacetime and shown that the \
throat is marginally connected.\\nIn the aforementioned range of parameters, \
the spacetime doesn't posses any\\nphoton orbit confirming the absence of \
shadow. We further analysed the\\nstability of this spacetime under scalar \
perturbation. Under the usual boundary\\nconditions (outgoing waves at both \
spatial infinities) there exists a\\ncontinuous spectra. On the contrary one \
may achieve the quantization of the\\nmodes by exploiting a different but \
physically intuitive boundary condition.\\nThe lowest lying mode behaves as \
normal mode, and the imaginary part comes into\\nplay for the modes \
corresponding to first overtone number $(n=1)$ marking the\\nonset of \
quasi-nomral modes for all azimuthal quantum number, $L$. We have \
also\\nargued that the spacetime has a tendency to hold the excitation in it \
due to\\nthe external perturbation, rather than a fast \
de-excitation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 11 Jul 2024 08:54:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-07-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Chatterjee\"", ",", "\"Soham\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Roy\"", ",", "\"Sagnik\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Koley\"", ",", "\"Ratna\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
