            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2407.08327\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Zihan Zhou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. V. S. Saketh, Zihan Zhou, Suprovo Ghosh, Jan \
Steinhoff, Debarati\\n  Chatterjee\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Investigating tidal heating in neutron stars via \
gravitational Raman\\n  scattering\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 2 tables, 1 appendix, version 2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"gr-qc astro-ph.HE hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a scattering amplitude formalism to study \
the tidal heating\\neffects of nonspinning neutron stars incorporating both \
worldline effective\\nfield theory and relativistic stellar perturbation \
theory. In neutron stars,\\ntidal heating arises from fluid viscosity due to \
various scattering processes\\nin the interior. It also serves as a channel \
for the exchange of energy and\\nangular momentum between the neutron star \
and its environment. In the interior\\nof the neutron star, we first derive \
two master perturbation equations that\\ncapture fluid perturbations accurate \
to linear order in frequency. Remarkably,\\nthese equations receive no \
contribution from bulk viscosity due to a peculiar\\nadiabatic \
incompressibility which arises in stellar fluid for \
non-barotropic\\nperturbations. In the exterior, the metric perturbations \
reduce to the\\nRegge-Wheeler (RW) equation which we solve using the \
analytical\\nMano-Suzuki-Takasugi (MST) method. We compute the amplitude for \
gravitational\\nwaves scattering off a neutron star, also known as \
gravitational Raman\\nscattering. From the amplitude, we obtain expressions \
for the electric\\nquadrupolar static Love number and the leading dissipation \
number to all orders\\nin compactness. We then compute the leading \
dissipation number for various\\nrealistic equation-of-state(s) and estimate \
the change in the number of\\ngravitational wave cycles due to tidal heating \
during inspiral in the\\nLIGO-Virgo-KAGRA (LVK) band.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 11 Jul 2024 09:26:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 26 Jul 2024 17:42:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
