               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We reconsider linear perturbations around general \
Friedmann - Lemaitre -\\nRobertson - Walker (FLRW) cosmological backgrounds. \
Exploiting gauge freedom\\ninvolving only time reparametrizations, we write \
down classical background\\nsolutions analytically, for an arbitrary number \
of fluid components. We then\\nshow that the time evolution of scalar and \
tensor adiabatic perturbations are\\ngoverned by Schr\\\\\\\"odinger-like \
differential equations of generalized Heun type.\\nAfter recovering known \
analytic results for a single-component fluid, we\\ndiscuss more general \
situations with two and three different fluid components,\\nwith special \
attention to the combination of radiation, matter and vacuum\\nenergy, which \
is supposed to describe the $\\\\Lambda$CDM model. The evolution of\\nlinear \
perturbations of a flat $\\\\Lambda$CDM universe is described by \
a\\ntwo-transient model, where the transitions from radiation to matter and \
matter\\nto vacuum energy are governed by a Heun equation and a \
Hypergeometric equation,\\nrespectively. We discuss an analytic approach to \
the study of the general case,\\ninvolving generalized Heun equations, that \
makes use of (quantum)\\nSeiberg-Witten curves for ${\\\\cal N}=2$ \
supersymmetric gauge theories and has\\nproven to be very effective in the \
analysis of Black-Hole, fuzzball and ECO\\nperturbations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 6 Aug 2024 15:05:24 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
