         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2408.03243", "submitter" -> "Giuseppe Dibitetto", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Massimo Bianchi, Giuseppe Dibitetto and Jose Francisco Morales", 
            "title" -> "Gauge theory meets cosmology", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 6 figures, 3 tables", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We reconsider linear perturbations around general Friedmann - \
Lemaitre -\nRobertson - Walker (FLRW) cosmological backgrounds. Exploiting \
gauge freedom\ninvolving only time reparametrizations, we write down \
classical background\nsolutions analytically, for an arbitrary number of \
fluid components. We then\nshow that the time evolution of scalar and tensor \
adiabatic perturbations are\ngoverned by Schr\\\"odinger-like differential \
equations of generalized Heun type.\nAfter recovering known analytic results \
for a single-component fluid, we\ndiscuss more general situations with two \
and three different fluid components,\nwith special attention to the \
combination of radiation, matter and vacuum\nenergy, which is supposed to \
describe the $\\Lambda$CDM model. The evolution of\nlinear perturbations of a \
flat $\\Lambda$CDM universe is described by a\ntwo-transient model, where the \
transitions from radiation to matter and matter\nto vacuum energy are \
governed by a Heun equation and a Hypergeometric equation,\nrespectively. We \
discuss an analytic approach to the study of the general case,\ninvolving \
generalized Heun equations, that makes use of (quantum)\nSeiberg-Witten \
curves for ${\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetric gauge theories and has\nproven to be \
very effective in the analysis of Black-Hole, fuzzball and ECO\n\
perturbations.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 6 Aug 2024 15:05:24 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-08-07", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bianchi", "Massimo", ""}, {
              "Dibitetto", "Giuseppe", ""}, {
              "Morales", "Jose Francisco", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
