               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2408.05208\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Frederic Jia\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hewei Frederic Jia, Mukund Rangamani\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic thermal correlators and quasinormal modes \
from semiclassical\\n  Virasoro blocks\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"69 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el gr-qc math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by its relevance for thermal correlators in \
strongly coupled\\nholographic CFTs, we refine and further develop a recent \
exact analytic\\napproach to black hole perturbation problem, based on the \
semiclassical\\nVirasoro blocks, or equivalently via AGT relation, the \
Nekrasov partition\\nfunctions in the Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit. Focusing on \
asymptotically\\n$\\\\text{AdS}_5$ black hole backgrounds, we derive new \
universal exact\\nexpressions for holographic thermal two-point functions, \
both for scalar\\noperators and conserved currents. Relatedly, we also obtain \
exact quantization\\nconditions of the associated quasinormal modes (QNMs). \
Our expressions for the\\nholographic $\\\\text{CFT}_4$ closely resemble the \
well-known results for 2d\\nthermal CFTs on $\\\\mathbb{R}^{1,1}$. This \
structural similarity stems from the\\nlocality of fusion transformation for \
Virasoro blocks. We provide numerical\\nchecks of our quantization conditions \
for QNMs. Additionally, we discuss the\\napplication of our results to \
understand specific physical properties of QNMs,\\nincluding their \
near-extremal and asymptotic limits. The latter is related to a\\ncertain \
large-momentum regime of semiclassical Virasoro blocks dual \
to\\nSeiberg-Witten prepotentials.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
