            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the wave form emitted by a particle moving along an \
arbitrary (in\ngeneral open) geodesic of the Schwarzschild geometry. The \
mathematical problem\ncan be phrased in terms of quantities in ${\\cal N}=2$ \
supersymmetric gauge\ntheories that can be calculated by using localization \
and the AGT\ncorrespondence. In particular through this mapping, the \
post-Newtonian\nexpansion of the wave form is expressed as a double instanton \
sum with rational\ncoefficients that resums all tail contributions into Gamma \
functions and\nexponentials. The formulae we obtain are valid for generic \
values of the\norbital quantum numbers $\\ell$ and $m$. For $\\ell=2,3$ we \
check explicitly that\nour results agree with the small mass ratio limit of \
the wave forms derived in\nthe Multipole Post-Minkowskian and the amplitudes \
approaches. We show how the\nso-called tail and tail of tail contributions to \
the wave form arise in our\napproach. Finally, we derive a universal formula \
for the soft limit of the wave\nform that resums all logarithmic divergent \
terms of the form $\\omega^{n-1}\n(\\log \\omega)^n$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
