                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study quasinormal modes of massive scalar \
perturbations in Kerr black\\nholes using the isomonodromic method. For \
arbitrary scalar masses $M \\\\mu$ and\\nblack hole spins $a/M$, we \
numerically determine the quasinormal frequencies\\nfor various orbital \
$\\\\ell$, azimuthal $m$, and overtone $n$ numbers. In\\nparticular, we \
derive an analytic expression for frequencies of the\\nzero-damping modes \
near the extremal limit $a/M \\\\rightarrow 1$. For $\\\\ell=m=1$,\\nwe \
reveal that the fundamental mode becomes a damped mode (rather than \
a\\nzero-damping mode) if the scalar field is sufficiently heavy. By \
exploring the\\nparameter space, we find numerical evidence for \
level-crossing between the\\nlongest-living mode and the first overtone at an \
exceptional point $(M\\\\mu)_c\\n\\\\simeq 0.3704981$ and $(a/M)_c\\\\simeq \
0.9994660$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
