            "  This paper investigates the normal modes of a probe scalar \
field in a\nfive-dimensional AdS-Schwarzschild black hole with the brick wall \
boundary\ncondition near the horizon. We employ various techniques to compute \
the\nspectrum and analyze its properties. Our results reveal a linear \
dependence of\nthe spectrum on the principal quantum number while \
demonstrating a non-trivial\ndependence on the angular momentum quantum \
number. We compute the Spectral Form\nFactor (SFF) and find a \
dip-ramp-plateau structure, with the slope of the ramp\napproaching unity as \
the brick wall nears the horizon. We also observe that as\nthe brick wall \
approaches the horizon, the poles of the retarded Green's\nfunction condense \
on the real line, leading to an emergent thermal behavior in\nthe boundary \
theory. This work extends previous studies on lower-dimensional\nblack holes \
to higher dimensions, providing insights into the connection\nbetween black \
hole microstate models and boundary chaos. Our findings\ncontribute to the \
ongoing discussions on the information paradox and the nature\nof black hole \
interiors in the context of AdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
