           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2409.11666", "submitter" -> "Di Wu", "authors" -> 
            "Wentao Liu, Li Zhang, Di Wu, Jieci Wang", "title" -> 
            "Thermodynamic topological classes of the rotating, accelerating \
black\n  holes", "comments" -> "28 pages, 9 figures, 1 table, JHEP3.cls", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper, we extend our previous work [D. Wu, Phys. Rev. \
D 108, 084041\n(2023)] to more general cases by including a rotation \
parameter. We investigate\nthe topological numbers for the rotating, \
accelerating neutral black hole and\nits AdS extension, as well as the \
rotating, accelerating charged black hole and\nits AdS extension. We find \
that the topological number of an asymptotically\nflat accelerating black \
hole consistently differs by one from that of its\nnon-accelerating \
counterpart. Furthermore, we show that for an asymptotically\nAdS \
accelerating black hole, the topological number is reduced by one compared\n\
to its non-accelerating AdS counterpart. In addition, we demonstrate that\n\
within the framework of general relativity, the acceleration parameter and \
the\nnegative cosmological constant each independently add one to the \
topological\nnumber. However, when both factors are present, their effects \
neutralize each\nother, resulting in no overall change to the topological \
number.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 18 Sep 2024 03:03:10 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-09-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Liu", "Wentao", ""}, {"Zhang", "Li", ""}, {
              "Wu", "Di", ""}, {"Wang", "Jieci", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
