               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2205.02256\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"David Grabovsky\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"David Berenstein, David Grabovsky, and Ziyi Li\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Aspects of Holography in Conical $AdS_3$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, 5 figures, JHEP style. v2: Section 4 was \
rewritten: an\\n  error was corrected that arose from using an approximation \
that did not\\n  apply. The crossing relations are now verified to all orders \
and do not\\n  present a puzzle any longer. The conclusions are updated based \
on the new\\n  calculations. Figures and references added. v3: Number of \
typos reduced.\\n  Supersedes the published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2023)029\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the Feynman propagator of free scalar fields \
in $AdS_3$ with a\\nconical defect. The propagator is built by solving the \
bulk equation of motion,\\nsumming over the modes of the field, and taking \
the boundary limit. We then\\nperform several consistency checks. In the dual \
CFT, the operator responsible\\nfor the defect creates a highly excited \
state. We consider the exchange of the\\nVirasoro identity block in the \
heavy-light limit to obtain an expression for\\nthe propagator sensitive to \
the mass of the defect. In $AdS_3/\\\\mathbb{Z}_n$, we\\ntreat the propagator \
by the method of images and in the geodesic approximation.\\nMore generally, \
we argue that long-range correlations of the scalar are\\nsuppressed as the \
defect becomes more massive: we find a continuous phase\\ntransition in the \
correlator at the BTZ threshold and examine its critical\\nbehavior. Finally, \
we apply our results to holographic entanglement entropy\\nusing an analogy \
between our scalars and replica twist fields.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
