            "  We study the Feynman propagator of free scalar fields in \
$AdS_3$ with a\nconical defect. The propagator is built by solving the bulk \
equation of motion,\nsumming over the modes of the field, and taking the \
boundary limit. We then\nperform several consistency checks. In the dual CFT, \
the operator responsible\nfor the defect creates a highly excited state. We \
consider the exchange of the\nVirasoro identity block in the heavy-light \
limit to obtain an expression for\nthe propagator sensitive to the mass of \
the defect. In $AdS_3/\\mathbb{Z}_n$, we\ntreat the propagator by the method \
of images and in the geodesic approximation.\nMore generally, we argue that \
long-range correlations of the scalar are\nsuppressed as the defect becomes \
more massive: we find a continuous phase\ntransition in the correlator at the \
BTZ threshold and examine its critical\nbehavior. Finally, we apply our \
results to holographic entanglement entropy\nusing an analogy between our \
scalars and replica twist fields.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
