 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Waveforms are classical observables associated with any \
radiative physical\\nprocess. Using scattering amplitudes, these are usually \
computed in a\\nweak-field regime to some finite order in the post-Newtonian \
or\\npost-Minkowskian approximation. Here, we use strong field amplitudes to \
compute\\nthe waveform produced in scattering of massive particles on \
gravitational plane\\nwaves, treated as exact nonlinear solutions of the \
vacuum Einstein equations.\\nNotably, the waveform contains an infinite \
number of post-Minkowskian\\ncontributions, as well as tail effects. We also \
provide, and contrast with,\\nanalogous results in \
electromagnetism.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
