               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tatsuya Hosoi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On Formal Series Solutions To 4th-order Quadratic \
Homogeneous\\n  Differential Equations And Their Convergence\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"9 pages, 0 figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math.CA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is known that all $\\\\tau$ functions of the Painlev\
\\\\'{e} equations satisfy\\nthe fourth-order quadratic differential \
equation. Among them, for the III, V,\\nand VI equations, it is possible to \
express the formal series solutions\\nexplicitly by using combinatorics. In \
this paper, we show the convergence of\\nthe formal series, including the \
solutions of more general equations. And by\\nthe absolute convergence of $\\\
\\tau $ series, the convergence of the conformal\\nblock function ($c=1$) \
also follows since it is a partial sum of the $\\\\tau $\\nseries. We also \
characterized the form of a homogeneous quadratic equation with\\na series \
solution similar to the tau functions of the Painlev\\\\'{e} equations.\\nThe \
Painlev\\\\'{e} equations are classified into six types, and it is known that\
\\nthey can be obtained by sequentially degenerating from type VI to type \
I.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
