for these\nrelations by considering two eigenvalue problems for the confluent \
Heun\nequations obtained from the linearized perturbation theory of black \
holes. We\nfirst derive the large frequency expansion of the spheroidal \
equations, and\nthen compare numerically the excited quasi-normal mode \
spectrum for the\nSchwarzschild case obtained from the large frequency \
expansion to the one\nobtained from the low frequency expansion and with the \
literature, indicating\nthat the relations hold generically in the complex \
modulus plane.\n", 
