 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute fully retarded scalar three-point functions \
of holographic CFTs at\\nfinite temperature using real-time holography. They \
describe the nonlinear\\nresponse of a holographic medium under scalar \
forcing, and display single and\\nhigher-order poles associated to resonant \
QNM excitations. This involves\\ncomputing the bulk-to-bulk propagator on a \
piecewise mixed-signature spacetime,\\nthe dual of the Schwinger-Keldysh \
contour. We show this construction is\\nequivalent to imposing ingoing \
boundary conditions on a single copy of a black\\nhole spacetime, similar to \
the case of the two-point function. We also compute\\nretarded scalar \
correlators with stress-tensor insertions in general CFTs by\\nsolving Ward \
identities on the Schwinger-Keldysh contour.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
