                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Massimo Bianchi, Giorgio Di Russo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"2-charge circular fuzz-balls and their \
perturbations\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"48 pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We perform a detailed study of perturbations around \
2-charge circular\\nfuzz-balls and compare the results with the ones obtained \
in the case of\\n'small' BHs. In addition to the photon-sphere modes that \
govern the prompt\\nring-down, we find a new branch of long-lived QNMs \
localised inside the\\nphoton-sphere at the (meta)stable minimum of the \
radial effective potential.\\nThe latter are expected to dominate late time \
signals in the form of 'echoes'.\\nMoreover, contrary to 'small' BHs, some \
'static' tidal Love numbers are\\nnon-zero and independent of the mass, \
charges and angular momentum of the\\nfuzz-ball. We rely on the recently \
established connection between BH or\\nfuzz-ball perturbation theory and \
quantum Seiberg-Witten curves for N = 2 SYM\\ntheories, which in turn are \
related to Liouville CFT via the AGT\\ncorrespondence. We test our results \
against numerical results obtained with\\nLeaver's method of continuous \
fractions or Breit-Wigner resonance method for\\ndirect integration and with \
the WKB approximation based on geodesic motion. We\\nalso exclude rotational \
super-radiance, due to the absence of an ergo-region,\\nand absorption, due \
to the absence of a horizon.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
