            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2212.07758\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Justin David R\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David, Srijan Kumar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermal one point functions, large $d$ and interior \
geometry of black\\n  holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, 4 figures, 1 table, reference added, typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2023)256\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study thermal one point functions of massive scalars \
in $AdS_{d+1}$ black\\nholes. These are induced by coupling the scalar to \
either the Weyl tensor\\nsquared or the Gauss-Bonnet term. Grinberg and \
Maldacena argued that the one\\npoint functions sourced by the Weyl tensor \
exponentiate in the limit of large\\nscalar masses and they contain \
information of the black hole geometry behind\\nthe horizon. We observe that \
the one point functions behave identically in this\\nlimit for either of the \
couplings mentioned earlier. We show that in an\\nappropriate large $d$ \
limit, the one point function for the charged black hole\\nin $AdS_{d+1}$ can \
be obtained exactly. These black holes in general contain an\\ninner horizon. \
We show that the one point function exponentiates and contains\\nthe \
information of both the proper time between the outer horizon to the \
inner\\nhorizon as well as the proper length from the inner horizon to the \
singularity.\\nWe also show that Gauss-Bonnet coupling induced one point \
functions in\\n$AdS_{d+1}$ black holes with hyperbolic horizons behave as \
anticipated by\\nGrinberg-Maldacena. Finally, we study the one point \
functions in the background\\nof rotating BTZ black holes induced by the \
cubic coupling of scalars.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
