            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study thermal one point functions of massive scalars in \
$AdS_{d+1}$ black\nholes. These are induced by coupling the scalar to either \
the Weyl tensor\nsquared or the Gauss-Bonnet term. Grinberg and Maldacena \
argued that the one\npoint functions sourced by the Weyl tensor exponentiate \
in the limit of large\nscalar masses and they contain information of the \
black hole geometry behind\nthe horizon. We observe that the one point \
functions behave identically in this\nlimit for either of the couplings \
mentioned earlier. We show that in an\nappropriate large $d$ limit, the one \
point function for the charged black hole\nin $AdS_{d+1}$ can be obtained \
exactly. These black holes in general contain an\ninner horizon. We show that \
the one point function exponentiates and contains\nthe information of both \
the proper time between the outer horizon to the inner\nhorizon as well as \
the proper length from the inner horizon to the singularity.\nWe also show \
that Gauss-Bonnet coupling induced one point functions in\n$AdS_{d+1}$ black \
holes with hyperbolic horizons behave as anticipated by\nGrinberg-Maldacena. \
Finally, we study the one point functions in the background\nof rotating BTZ \
black holes induced by the cubic coupling of scalars.\n", 
