                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Using the AdS/CFT correspondence we model the \
behaviour of the two point\\ncorrelator of an operator with arbitrary scale \
dimension $\\\\Delta$ in arbitrary\\nspacetime dimension $d$ for small but \
non-zero temperature. The obtained\\npropagator coincides in the low \
temperature regime with the known result for\\n$d=4$ for large $\\\\Delta$ at \
the order $T^d$ as well as with the $T^d$ and\\n$T^{2d}$ terms of the exact \
all order result for $d=2$. Furthermore, for\\narbitrary $d$ we explicitly \
write down the expression for the order $T^{d}$ of\\nthe propagator for \
arbitrary $\\\\Delta$, and present a conjecture for the order\\n$T^{2d}$ in \
the large $\\\\Delta$ limit.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
