 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The aim of this paper is to study the effect of \
isomonodromic deformations of\\nthe evolution of scalar fields in \
Sasaki-Einstein spaces in the context of\\nholography. Here we analyze the \
monodromy data of the general Heun equation,\\nresulting from a scalar on \
Y$^{p,q}$, thus obtaining the corresponding\\nPainlev\\\\'e VI equation. \
Furthermore we have considered limits leading to a\\ncoalescence of \
singularities, which in turn transform the original Painlev\\\\'e\\nVI \
equation, to one of lower rank. The confluent limits we have considered \
are\\nY$^{p,p}$, T$^{1,1} / \\\\mathbb{Z}_2$ and Y$^{\\\\infty, \
q}$.\\n\""}]}, {
