               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pratik Nandy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Aranya Bhattacharya, Pratik Nandy, Pingal Pratyush Nath, \
Himanshu Sahu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On Krylov complexity in open systems: an approach via \
bi-Lanczos\\n  algorithm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: some sections added and updated, clarifications \
added, published\\n  version in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 12 (2023) 066\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2023)066\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"YITP-23-25\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"quant-ph cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.str-el hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Continuing the previous initiatives arXiv: 2207.05347 \
and arXiv: 2212.06180,\\nwe pursue the exploration of operator growth and \
Krylov complexity in\\ndissipative open quantum systems. In this paper, we \
resort to the bi-Lanczos\\nalgorithm generating two bi-orthogonal Krylov \
spaces, which individually\\ngenerate non-orthogonal subspaces. Unlike the \
previously studied Arnoldi\\niteration, this algorithm renders the \
Lindbladian into a purely tridiagonal\\nform, thus opening up a possibility \
to study a wide class of dissipative\\nintegrable and chaotic systems by \
computing Krylov complexity at late times.\\nOur study relies on two specific \
systems, the dissipative transverse-field\\nIsing model (TFIM) and the \
dissipative interacting XXZ chain. We find that, for\\nthe weak coupling, \
initial Lanczos coefficients can efficiently distinguish\\nintegrable and \
chaotic evolution before the dissipative effect sets in, which\\nresults in \
more fluctuations in higher Lanczos coefficients. This results in\\nthe equal \
saturation of late-time complexity for both integrable and chaotic\\ncases, \
making the notion of late-time chaos dubious.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 7 Mar 2023 19:00:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
