            "Massimo Bianchi, Maurizio Firrotta, Jacob Sonnenschein, Dorin \
Weissman", "title" -> "Measuring chaos in string scattering processes", 
            "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.CD", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyze the amplitudes of one highly excited string (HES) \
state with two\nor three tachyons in open bosonic string theory. We argue \
that these processes\nare chaotic by showing that the spacing ratios of \
successive peaks in the\nangular dependence of the amplitudes are distributed \
as predicted by the\n$\\beta$-ensemble of random matrix theory (RMT). We show \
how the continuous\nparameter $\\beta$ depends on the level and helicity of \
the scattered HES state.\nWe derive the scattering amplitude of an HES and \
three tachyons and show that\nit takes the form of the Veneziano amplitude \
times a dressing factor, and that\nthe dressing is chaotic as a function of \
the scattering angle, in the sense\nthat its spacing ratios match with RMT \
predictions.\n", 
