               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We reduce the study of perturbations of rotating black \
holes in\\nhigher-derivative extensions of general relativity to a system of \
decoupled\\nradial equations that stem from a set of universal Teukolsky \
equations. We\\ndetail a complete computational strategy to obtain these \
decoupled equations in\\ngeneral higher-derivative theories. We apply this to \
six-derivative gravity to\\ncompute the shifts in the quasinormal mode \
frequencies with respect to those of\\nKerr black holes in general \
relativity. At linear order in the angular momentum\\nwe reproduce earlier \
results obtained with a metric perturbation approach. In\\ncontrast with this \
earlier work, however, the method given here applies also to\\npost-merger \
black holes with significant spin, which are of particular\\nobservational \
interest.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
