            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2304.08824\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Qianhang Ding\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ali Akil, Qianhang Ding\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A Dark Matter Probe in Accreting Pulsar-Black Hole \
Binaries\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"15 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"astro-ph.HE astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The accretion of dark matter (DM) into astrophysical \
black holes slowly\\nincreases their mass. The rate of this mass accretion \
depends on the DM model\\nand the model parameters. If this mass accretion \
effect can be measured\\naccurately enough, it is possible to rule out some \
DM models, and, with the\\nsufficient technology and the help of other DM \
constraints, possibly confirm\\none model. We propose a DM probe based on \
accreting pulsar-black hole binaries,\\nwhich provide a high-precision \
measurement on binary orbital phase shifts\\ninduced by DM accretion into \
black holes, and can help rule out DM models and\\nstudy the nature of DM.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
