         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2304.08824", "submitter" -> "Qianhang Ding", "authors" -> 
            "Ali Akil, Qianhang Ding", "title" -> 
            "A Dark Matter Probe in Accreting Pulsar-Black Hole Binaries", 
            "comments" -> "15 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "astro-ph.HE astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The accretion of dark matter (DM) into astrophysical black \
holes slowly\nincreases their mass. The rate of this mass accretion depends \
on the DM model\nand the model parameters. If this mass accretion effect can \
be measured\naccurately enough, it is possible to rule out some DM models, \
and, with the\nsufficient technology and the help of other DM constraints, \
possibly confirm\none model. We propose a DM probe based on accreting \
pulsar-black hole binaries,\nwhich provide a high-precision measurement on \
binary orbital phase shifts\ninduced by DM accretion into black holes, and \
can help rule out DM models and\nstudy the nature of DM.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 18 Apr 2023 08:43:22 GMT"}, {
