               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2304.14035\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Piyabut Burikham\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Byon N. Jayawiguna, Piyabut Burikham\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gravitational Perturbation in Nonlocal Modified Tolman \
VII Model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, 12 figures, 4 tables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In comparison to the original Tolman VII model, Exact \
Modified Tolman VII\\n(EMTVII) with one additional parameter can increase the \
compactness of compact\\nobject. When the compactness is in the ultracompact \
regime, the quasinormal\\nmodes~(QNMs) of the trapped mode as well as the \
gravitational echoes become\\nmore viable. Starting with the EMTVII model, we \
introduce nonlocality into the\\nmatter sector and analyze the effective \
potential, the QNMs, and the\\ngravitational echoes of the compact and \
ultracompact object in the nonlocal\\nmodel. The nonlocal gravity version of \
EMTVII~(NEMTVII) is parametrized by the\\nnonlocal parameter~($ \\\\beta $), \
modified Tolman VII parameter ($ \\\\alpha $), and\\nthe compactness ($ \
\\\\mathcal{C}$). It is found that the nonlocal profile\\nproduces the \
smeared surface and consequently reduce the compactness. The\\nmaximum \
compactness $\\\\mathcal{C}_{max}=0.4$ occurs when $\\\\alpha=0=\\\\beta$, \
i.e.,\\nEMTVII with no smearing. For relatively small value of $\\\\beta = \
0.01$ and the\\ncompactness $ \\\\mathcal{C} \\\\lesssim 0.2667$~(with \
$M=2.14$ solar masses,\\n$R=11.835$ km at $\\\\alpha=1.4$), the causality \
condition and the dominant energy\\ncondition~(DEC) are satisfied. The \
quasinormal modes of the gravitational\\nperturbation are calculated using \
Bohr-Sommerfeld (BS) fitting and we find that\\nthe nonlocality produces less \
trapped modes than the original (EMTVII)\\ncounterpart. At high compactness, \
gravitational echoes are simulated\\nnumerically. Echoes are found to exist \
in the parameter space where the\\ndominant energy condition and the \
causality condition are violated.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
