               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2304.14173\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vaios Ziogas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Baggioli, Yanyan Bu, and Vaios Ziogas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"U(1) quasi-hydrodynamics: Schwinger-Keldysh effective \
field theory and\\n  holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v3: matches published version, v2: new subsection, \
references added,\\n  minor edits; v1: 44 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP09(2023)019\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2023)019\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CPHT-RR017.042023\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el nucl-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the quasi-hydrodynamics of a system with a \
softly broken $U(1)$\\nglobal symmetry using effective field theory (EFT) and \
holographic methods. In\\nthe gravity side, we consider a holographic Proca \
model in the limit of small\\nbulk mass, which is responsible for a \
controllable explicit breaking of the\\n$U(1)$ global symmetry in the \
boundary field theory. We perform a holographic\\nSchwinger-Keldysh analysis, \
which allows us to derive the form of the boundary\\neffective action in \
presence of dissipation. We compare our results with the\\npreviously \
proposed EFT and hydrodynamic theories, and we confirm their\\nvalidity by \
computing the low-energy quasi-normal modes spectrum analytically\\nand \
numerically. Additionally, we derive the broken holographic Ward \
identity\\nfor the $U(1)$ current, and discuss the recently proposed novel \
transport\\ncoefficients for systems with explicitly broken symmetries. The \
setup\\nconsidered is expected to serve as a toy model for more realistic \
situations\\nwhere quasi-hydrodynamics is at work, such as axial charge \
relaxation in QCD,\\nspin relaxation in relativistic systems, electric field \
relaxation in\\nmagneto-hydrodynamics, or momentum relaxation in condensed \
matter systems.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
