         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2304.14173", "submitter" -> "Vaios Ziogas", "authors" -> 
            "Matteo Baggioli, Yanyan Bu, and Vaios Ziogas", "title" -> 
            "U(1) quasi-hydrodynamics: Schwinger-Keldysh effective field \
theory and\n  holography", "comments" -> 
            "v3: matches published version, v2: new subsection, references \
added,\n  minor edits; v1: 44 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP09(2023)019", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP09(2023)019", 
            "report-no" -> "CPHT-RR017.042023", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.str-el nucl-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the quasi-hydrodynamics of a system with a softly \
broken $U(1)$\nglobal symmetry using effective field theory (EFT) and \
holographic methods. In\nthe gravity side, we consider a holographic Proca \
model in the limit of small\nbulk mass, which is responsible for a \
controllable explicit breaking of the\n$U(1)$ global symmetry in the boundary \
field theory. We perform a holographic\nSchwinger-Keldysh analysis, which \
allows us to derive the form of the boundary\neffective action in presence of \
dissipation. We compare our results with the\npreviously proposed EFT and \
hydrodynamic theories, and we confirm their\nvalidity by computing the \
low-energy quasi-normal modes spectrum analytically\nand numerically. \
Additionally, we derive the broken holographic Ward identity\nfor the $U(1)$ \
current, and discuss the recently proposed novel transport\ncoefficients for \
systems with explicitly broken symmetries. The setup\nconsidered is expected \
to serve as a toy model for more realistic situations\nwhere \
quasi-hydrodynamics is at work, such as axial charge relaxation in QCD,\nspin \
relaxation in relativistic systems, electric field relaxation in\n\
magneto-hydrodynamics, or momentum relaxation in condensed matter systems.\n",
             "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 27 Apr 2023 13:21:15 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 16 May 2023 10:40:08 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 27 Aug 2023 22:33:36 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-09-07", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Baggioli", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "Bu", "Yanyan", ""}, {"Ziogas", "Vaios", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
