 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For any (possibly singular) hyperelliptic curve, we \
give the definition of a\\nhyperelliptic refined spectral curve and the \
hyperelliptic refined topological\\nrecursion, generalising the formulation \
for a special class of genus-zero\\ncurves by Kidwai and the author, and also \
improving the proposal by Chekhov and\\nEynard. Along the way, we uncover a \
fundamental geometric structure underlying\\nthe hyperelliptic refined \
topological recursion and investigate its properties\\n-- parts of which \
remain conjectural due to computational difficulties.\\nMoreover, we \
establish a new recursion valid in the so-called\\nNekrasov-Shatashivili \
limit and prove existence of the corresponding quantum\\ncurve.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
