 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  AGT conjecture reveals a connection between 4D \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ gauge theory\\nand 2D conformal field theory. Though some \
special instances have been proven,\\nothers remain elusive and the attempts \
on its full proof never stop. When the\\n$\\\\Omega$ background parameters \
satisfy $-\\\\epsilon_1/\\\\epsilon_2\\\\equiv \\\\beta =1$,\\nthe story \
simplifies a bit. A proof of the correspondence in the case of\\n$A_{1}$ \
gauge group was given in 2010 by Mironov et al., while the \
$A_{n}$\\nextension is verified by Matsuo and Zhang in 2011, with an \
assumption on the\\nSelberg integral of $n+1$ Schur polynomials. Then in \
2020, Albion et al.\\nobtained the rigorous result of this formula. In this \
paper, we show that their\\nresult is equivalent to the conjecture on Selberg \
integral of Schur\\npolynomials, thus leading to the proof of the $A_{n}$ \
case at $\\\\beta=1$. To\\nperform a double check, we also directly start \
from this formula, and manage to\\nshow the identification between the two \
sides of AGT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
