                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive an effective action for charged plasmas with \
an anomalous (abelian)\\nglobal current charge current using holography. The \
holographic description is\\ncaptured by the dynamics of an \
Einstein-Maxwell-Chern-Simons theory in an\\nasymptotically AdS spacetime. \
The 't Hooft anomaly contribution, which is\\nencoded in the Chern-Simons \
term, contributes at the Gaussian order in the\\neffective action only in the \
momentum diffusion sector, where it leads to\\nchiral shear waves. However, \
as we demonstrate, beyond the Gaussian order,\\nthere is a non-trivial \
imprint of the parity-violating anomaly term in sound\\nand charge diffusion \
dynamics as well.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
