         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2306.01055", "submitter" -> "Mukund Rangamani", "authors" -> 
            "Mukund Rangamani, Julio Virrueta, Shuyan Zhou", "title" -> 
            "Anomalous hydrodynamics effective actions from holography", 
            "comments" -> "v2: minor improvements (published version)", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive an effective action for charged plasmas with an \
anomalous (abelian)\nglobal current charge current using holography. The \
holographic description is\ncaptured by the dynamics of an \
Einstein-Maxwell-Chern-Simons theory in an\nasymptotically AdS spacetime. The \
't Hooft anomaly contribution, which is\nencoded in the Chern-Simons term, \
contributes at the Gaussian order in the\neffective action only in the \
momentum diffusion sector, where it leads to\nchiral shear waves. However, as \
we demonstrate, beyond the Gaussian order,\nthere is a non-trivial imprint of \
the parity-violating anomaly term in sound\nand charge diffusion dynamics as \
well.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 1 Jun 2023 18:01:01 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
