, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Conformal theories of the Argyres-Douglas type are \
notoriously hard to study\\ngiven that they are isolated and strongly coupled \
thus lacking a lagrangian\\ndescription. In flat space, an exact description \
is provided by the\\nSeiberg-Witten theory. Turning on a \
$\\\\Omega$-background makes the geometry\\n``quantum\\\" and tractable only \
in the weak curvature limit. In this paper we use\\nthe AGT correspondence to \
derive $\\\\Omega$-exact formulae for the partition\\nfunction, in the nearby \
of monopole points where the dynamics is described by\\nirregular conformal \
blocks of the CFT. The results are checked against those\\nobtained by the \
recursion relations coming from a conformal anomaly in the\\nregion where the \
two approaches overlap. The Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit is also\\ndiscussed. \
Finally, we comment on the existence of black holes in De Sitter\\nspace \
whose low energy dynamics is described by an Argyres-Douglas \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
