            "id" -> "2306.05127", "submitter" -> "Francesco Fucito", 
             "authors" -> 
             "Francesco Fucito, Jose Francisco Morales, Rubik Poghossian", 
             "title" -> "On irregular states and Argyres-Douglas theories", 
             "comments" -> 
             "26 pages, 1 reference added, many typos corrected as suggested \
from\n  the referee", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
             Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Conformal theories of the Argyres-Douglas type are \
notoriously hard to study\ngiven that they are isolated and strongly coupled \
thus lacking a lagrangian\ndescription. In flat space, an exact description \
is provided by the\nSeiberg-Witten theory. Turning on a $\\Omega$-background \
makes the geometry\n``quantum\" and tractable only in the weak curvature \
limit. In this paper we use\nthe AGT correspondence to derive $\\Omega$-exact \
formulae for the partition\nfunction, in the nearby of monopole points where \
the dynamics is described by\nirregular conformal blocks of the CFT. The \
results are checked against those\nobtained by the recursion relations coming \
from a conformal anomaly in the\nregion where the two approaches overlap. The \
Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit is also\ndiscussed. Finally, we comment on the \
existence of black holes in De Sitter\nspace whose low energy dynamics is \
described by an Argyres-Douglas theory.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 8 Jun 2023 11:51:02 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 28 Jun 2023 14:15:12 GMT"}, {
