                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  When a (super) conformal field theory is placed on a \
non-trivial manifold,\\nthe (super) conformal symmetry is broken. However, it \
is still possible to\\nderive broken Ward identities for these broken \
symmetries, which provide\\nadditional constraints on the theory. We derive \
and apply the broken Ward\\nidentities associated with the (super) conformal \
group on the thermal manifold\\n$\\\\mathcal{M}_\\\\beta = S_\\\\beta^1 \
\\\\times \\\\mathbb{R}^{d-1}$ and $\\\\mathcal{M} = T^2\\n\\\\times \
\\\\mathbb{R}^{d-2}$. The novel constraints not only \
systematically\\nreproduce known results, including an implicit formulation \
of the generalized\\nCardy formula, but also elegantly relate the thermal \
energy spectrum with the\\nconformal spectrum.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
