               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Topological defect lines (TDLs) are extended line \
operators which act on the\\nHilbert space of two-dimensional CFTs and \
satisfy non-trivial fusion algebras\\nwhen forming junctions. Among the most \
interesting fusion algebras are the\\nso-called Tambara-Yamagami (TY) fusion \
categories which are realized in\\n(bosonized) Parafermionic CFTs. The \
corresponding TY[$\\\\mathbb{Z}_k$]-categories\\nhave been explicitly \
realized for the cases $k=2$, $k=3$, and $k=4$ together\\nwith the action of \
the defect lines on the Hilbert space of the corresponding\\nCFTs. For each \
of the cases, different methods have been used in the previous\\nliterature. \
In the current paper, we present a unified framework for finding\\nthe TDLs \
in bosonized Parafermionic CFTs. Our approach relies on combining\\nseveral \
previously used methods and the definition of an extended $S$ matrix.\\nWe \
apply the method to the cases $k=2$ to $k=5$ to extract corresponding \
TDL\\nfusion algebras.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
