                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Photon spheres are the characteristic of general black \
holes, thus are a\\nsuitable touchstone for the emergence of gravitational \
spacetime in the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. We provide a spectral analysis of \
an AdS Schwarzschild black\\nhole near its photon sphere. We find that \
quasinormal modes near the photon\\nsphere reflect the AdS boundary, \
resulting in a peculiar spectral pattern. Our\\nlarge angular momentum \
analysis owes to an analogue to solvable Schr\\\\\\\"odinger\\nequations such \
as an inverted harmonic oscillator and the P\\\\\\\"oschl-Teller\\nmodel, \
with a Dirichlet boundary condition. Through the AdS/CFT dictionary, \
it\\npredicts the existence of a peculiar subsector in the large angular \
momentum\\nspectrum of thermal holographic CFTs on a sphere.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
