thus are a\nsuitable touchstone for the emergence of gravitational spacetime \
in the AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence. We provide a spectral analysis of an AdS \
Schwarzschild black\nhole near its photon sphere. We find that quasinormal \
modes near the photon\nsphere reflect the AdS boundary, resulting in a \
peculiar spectral pattern. Our\nlarge angular momentum analysis owes to an \
analogue to solvable Schr\\\"odinger\nequations such as an inverted harmonic \
oscillator and the P\\\"oschl-Teller\nmodel, with a Dirichlet boundary \
condition. Through the AdS/CFT dictionary, it\npredicts the existence of a \
peculiar subsector in the large angular momentum\nspectrum of thermal \
holographic CFTs on a sphere.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 1 Jul 2023 05:58:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-07-04", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hashimoto", "Koji", ""}, {
              "Sugiura", "Kakeru", ""}, {"Sugiyama", "Katsuyuki", ""}, {
              "Yoda", "Takuya", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
