                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We apply the exact WKB analysis to a couple of \
one-dimensional\\nSchroedinger-type equations reduced from the Stark effect \
of hydrogen in a\\nuniform electric field. By introducing Langer's \
modification and incorporating\\nthe Stokes graphs, we prove the exactness of \
the Bohr-Sommerfeld quantization\\nconditions for the Borel-resummed quantum \
WKB periods in the specific parameter\\nregions of the electric field \
intensity and magnetic quantum number. It is also\\nfound these quantization \
conditions get modified with an additional suppressed\\ncontribution when the \
parameters vary beyond the specific regions. We also\\npresent Thermodynamic \
Bethe Ansatz (TBA) equations governing the quantum\\nperiods in the absence \
of Langer's modification and discuss its wall-crossing\\nand analytic \
continuation. Numerical calculations are conducted to compare the\\ncomplex \
resonant frequencies from our quantization conditions against ones from\\nthe \
Riccati-Pade method, the TBA equations are also confirmed by comparing \
its\\nexpansions with all-order quantum periods.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
