            "  Ultralight bosons are well-motivated particles from various \
physical and\ncosmological theories, and can be spontaneously produced during \
the\nsuperradiant process, forming a dense hydrogen-like cloud around the \
spinning\nblack hole. After the growth saturates, the cloud slowly depletes \
its mass\nthrough gravitational-wave emission. In this work we study the \
orbit dynamics\nof a binary system containing such a gravitational atom \
saturated in various\nspin-0,1,2 superradiant states, taking into account \
both the effects of\ndynamical friction and the cloud mass depletion. We \
estimate the significance\nof mass depletion, finding that although dynamical \
friction could dominate the\ninspiral phase, it typically does not affect the \
outspiral phase driven by the\nmass depletion. Focusing on the large orbit \
radius, we investigate the\ncondition to observe the outspiral, and the \
detectability of the cloud via\npulsar-timing signal in the case of black \
hole-pulsar binary.\n", 
