 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the spectrum of linearized gravitational \
excitations of black\\nholes with substantial angular momentum in the \
presence of higher-derivative\\ncorrections to general relativity. We do so \
perturbatively to leading order in\\nthe higher-derivative couplings and up \
to order fourteen in the black hole\\nangular momentum. This allows us to \
accurately predict quasinormal mode\\nfrequencies of black holes with spins \
up to about $70\\\\%$ of the extremal value.\\nFor some higher-derivative \
corrections, we find that sizable rotation enhances\\nthe frequency shifts by \
almost an order of magnitude relative to the static\\ncase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
