                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gleb Aminov\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Gleb Aminov, Paolo Arnaudo, Giulio Bonelli, Alba Grassi, \
Alessandro\\n  Tanzini\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Black hole perturbation theory and multiple \
polylogarithms\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Version 2 has 58 pages, 3 figures, and 4 Mathematica \
files. Minor\\n  corrections added. Comments welcome\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"J. High Energ. Phys. 2023, 59 (2023)\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2023)059\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study black hole linear perturbation theory in a \
four-dimensional\\nSchwarzschild (anti) de Sitter background. When dealing \
with a positive\\ncosmological constant, the corresponding spectral problem \
is solved\\nsystematically via the Nekrasov-Shatashvili functions or, \
equivalently,\\nclassical Virasoro conformal blocks. However, this approach \
can be more\\ncomplicated to implement for certain perturbations if the \
cosmological constant\\nis negative. For these cases, we propose an \
alternative method to set up\\nperturbation theory for both small and large \
black holes in an analytical\\nmanner. Our analysis reveals a new underlying \
recursive structure that involves\\nmultiple polylogarithms. We focus on \
gravitational, electromagnetic, and\\nconformally coupled scalar \
perturbations subject to Dirichlet and Robin\\nboundary conditions. The \
low-lying modes of the scalar sector of gravitational\\nperturbations and its \
hydrodynamic limit are studied in detail.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
