          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "2307.10141", "submitter" -> "Gleb Aminov", "authors" -> 
             "Gleb Aminov, Paolo Arnaudo, Giulio Bonelli, Alba Grassi, \
Alessandro\n  Tanzini", "title" -> 
             "Black hole perturbation theory and multiple polylogarithms", 
             "comments" -> 
             "Version 2 has 58 pages, 3 figures, and 4 Mathematica files. \
Minor\n  corrections added. Comments welcome", "journal-ref" -> 
             "J. High Energ. Phys. 2023, 59 (2023)", "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP11(2023)059", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study black hole linear perturbation theory in a \
four-dimensional\nSchwarzschild (anti) de Sitter background. When dealing \
with a positive\ncosmological constant, the corresponding spectral problem is \
solved\nsystematically via the Nekrasov-Shatashvili functions or, \
equivalently,\nclassical Virasoro conformal blocks. However, this approach \
can be more\ncomplicated to implement for certain perturbations if the \
cosmological constant\nis negative. For these cases, we propose an \
alternative method to set up\nperturbation theory for both small and large \
black holes in an analytical\nmanner. Our analysis reveals a new underlying \
recursive structure that involves\nmultiple polylogarithms. We focus on \
gravitational, electromagnetic, and\nconformally coupled scalar perturbations \
subject to Dirichlet and Robin\nboundary conditions. The low-lying modes of \
the scalar sector of gravitational\nperturbations and its hydrodynamic limit \
are studied in detail.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 19 Jul 2023 17:10:16 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 16 Nov 2023 16:54:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2023-11-17", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Aminov", "Gleb", ""}, {
               "Arnaudo", "Paolo", ""}, {"Bonelli", "Giulio", ""}, {
               "Grassi", "Alba", ""}, {"Tanzini", "Alessandro", ""}}}], 
           "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
