             "  We often encounter a situation that black hole solutions can \
be regarded as\ncontinuous deformations of simpler ones, or modify general \
relativity by\ncontinuous parameters. We develop a general framework to \
compute high-order\nperturbative corrections to quasinormal mode frequencies \
in such deformed\nproblems. Our method has many applications, and allows to \
compute numerical\nvalues of the high-order corrections very accurately. For \
several examples, we\nperform this computation explicitly, and discuss \
analytic properties of the\nquasinormal mode frequencies for deformation \
parameters.\n", 
