             "abstract" -> 
             "  The holographic gauge/gravity duality provides an explicit \
reduction of\nquantum field theory (QFT) calculations in the semi-classical \
large-$N$ limit\nto sets of `gravitational' differential equations whose \
analysis can reveal all\ndetails of the spectra of thermal QFT correlators. \
We argue that in certain\ncases, a complete reconstruction of the spectrum \
and of the corresponding\ncorrelator is possible from only the knowledge of \
an infinite, discrete set of\npole-skipping points traversed by a single \
(hydrodynamic) mode computed in a\nseries expansion in an inverse number of \
spacetime dimensions. Conceptually,\nthis reduces the computation of a QFT \
correlator spectrum to performing a set\nof purely algebraic manipulations. \
With the help of the pole-skipping analysis,\nwe also uncover a novel \
structure underpinning the coefficients that enter the\nhydrodynamic \
dispersion relations.\n", 
