 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study 4d type ${\\\\cal H}_0$ Argyres-Douglas theory \
in $\\\\Omega$-background\\nby constructing Liouville irregular state of rank \
5/2. The results are compared\\nwith generalized Holomorphic anomaly \
approach, which provides order by order\\nexpansion in $\\\\Omega$-background \
parameters $\\\\epsilon_{1,2}$. Another crucial\\ntest of our results \
provides comparison with respect to Painlev\\\\'{e} 1\\n$\\\\tau$-function, \
which was expected to be hold in self-dual \
case\\n$\\\\epsilon_1=-\\\\epsilon_2$. We also discuss Nekrasov-Shatashvili \
limit\\n$\\\\epsilon_1=0$, accessible either by means of deformed \
Seiberg-Witten curve, or\\nWKB methods.\\n\""}]}, {
