               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ye-Sheng Xue, Jie Jiang, Ming Zhang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Notes on emergent conformal symmetry for black \
holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 2 figures. v2: section 3 added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We examine the motion of the massless scalar field and \
nearly bound null\\ngeodesics in the near-ring region of a black hole, which \
may possess either\\nacceleration or a gravitomagnetic mass. Around such \
black holes, the photon\\nring deviates from the equatorial plane. In the \
large angular momentum limit,\\nwe demonstrate that the massless scalar field \
exhibits an emergent conformal\\nsymmetry in this near-ring region. \
Additionally, in the nearly bound limit, we\\nobserve the emergence of a \
conformal symmetry for the null geodesics that\\nconstitute the photon ring \
in the black hole image. These findings suggest that\\nthe hidden conformal \
symmetry, associated with the Lie algebra $\\\\mathfrak{s\\nl}(2, \
\\\\mathbb{R})$, persists even for black holes lacking \
north-south\\nreflection symmetry, thereby broadening the foundation of \
photon ring\\nholography. Finally, we show that the conformal symmetry also \
emerges for\\nnearly bound timelike geodesics and scalar fields in proximity \
to the particle\\nring, and with specific mass around a Schwarzschild black \
hole.\\n\""}]}, {
