            "  We examine the motion of the massless scalar field and nearly \
bound null\ngeodesics in the near-ring region of a black hole, which may \
possess either\nacceleration or a gravitomagnetic mass. Around such black \
holes, the photon\nring deviates from the equatorial plane. In the large \
angular momentum limit,\nwe demonstrate that the massless scalar field \
exhibits an emergent conformal\nsymmetry in this near-ring region. \
Additionally, in the nearly bound limit, we\nobserve the emergence of a \
conformal symmetry for the null geodesics that\nconstitute the photon ring in \
the black hole image. These findings suggest that\nthe hidden conformal \
symmetry, associated with the Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{s\nl}(2, \\mathbb{R})$, \
persists even for black holes lacking north-south\nreflection symmetry, \
thereby broadening the foundation of photon ring\nholography. Finally, we \
show that the conformal symmetry also emerges for\nnearly bound timelike \
geodesics and scalar fields in proximity to the particle\nring, and with \
specific mass around a Schwarzschild black hole.\n", 
