           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2309.05559\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Felipe Diaz\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Adolfo Cisterna, Felipe Diaz, Robert B. Mann, Julio \
Oliva\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Exploring Accelerating Hairy Black Holes in $2+1$ \
Dimensions: The\\n  Asymptotically Locally Anti-de Sitter Class and its \
Holography\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"45 pages, 17 figures, 3 tables. Published version\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP11(2023)073\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2023)073\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In the realm of lower-dimensional accelerating \
spacetimes, it is\\nwell-established that the presence of domain walls, which \
are co-dimension one\\ntopological defects, is a necessary condition for \
their construction. We expand\\nthe geometric framework by adding a \
conformally coupled scalar field. This\\nendeavor leads to the identification \
of several new families of\\nthree-dimensional accelerating spacetimes with \
asymptotically locally anti-de\\nSitter (AdS) behavior. Notably, one of these \
solutions showcases a hairy\\ngeneralization of the accelerating BTZ black \
hole. This solution is constructed\\nat both slow and rapid phases of \
acceleration, and its connection with\\nestablished vacuum spacetime models \
is explicitly elucidated. The inclusion of\\nthe scalar field imparts a \
non-constant Ricci curvature to the domain wall,\\nthereby rendering these \
configurations particularly suitable for the\\nconstruction of \
two-dimensional quantum black holes. To establish a well-posed\\nvariational \
principle in the presence of the domain wall, two essential steps\\nare \
undertaken. First, we extend the conventional renormalized AdS$_3$ \
action\\nto accommodate the presence of the scalar field. Second, to \
establish a\\nwell-posed variational principle, we extend the renormalized \
AdS$_3$ action to\\ninclude the scalar field and incorporate the \
Gibbons--Hawking--York term for\\ninternal boundaries and domain wall \
tension. We engage in holographic\\ncomputations, thereby determining the \
explicit form of the holographic stress\\ntensor. In this context, the stress \
tensor can be expressed as that of a\\nperfect fluid situated on a curved \
background. Additionally, it paves the road\\nto ascertain the spacetime \
mass. Finally, we close by demonstrating the\\nexistence of three-dimensional \
accelerating spacetimes with asymptotically\\nlocally flat and asymptotically \
locally de Sitter geometries, particularly\\nthose embodying black \
holes.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
