          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "2309.05559", "submitter" -> "Felipe Diaz", "authors" -> 
             "Adolfo Cisterna, Felipe Diaz, Robert B. Mann, Julio Oliva", 
             "title" -> 
             "Exploring Accelerating Hairy Black Holes in $2+1$ Dimensions: \
The\n  Asymptotically Locally Anti-de Sitter Class and its Holography", 
             "comments" -> 
             "45 pages, 17 figures, 3 tables. Published version", 
             "journal-ref" -> "JHEP11(2023)073", "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP11(2023)073", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
             "  In the realm of lower-dimensional accelerating spacetimes, it \
is\nwell-established that the presence of domain walls, which are \
co-dimension one\ntopological defects, is a necessary condition for their \
construction. We expand\nthe geometric framework by adding a conformally \
coupled scalar field. This\nendeavor leads to the identification of several \
new families of\nthree-dimensional accelerating spacetimes with \
asymptotically locally anti-de\nSitter (AdS) behavior. Notably, one of these \
solutions showcases a hairy\ngeneralization of the accelerating BTZ black \
hole. This solution is constructed\nat both slow and rapid phases of \
acceleration, and its connection with\nestablished vacuum spacetime models is \
explicitly elucidated. The inclusion of\nthe scalar field imparts a \
non-constant Ricci curvature to the domain wall,\nthereby rendering these \
configurations particularly suitable for the\nconstruction of two-dimensional \
quantum black holes. To establish a well-posed\nvariational principle in the \
presence of the domain wall, two essential steps\nare undertaken. First, we \
extend the conventional renormalized AdS$_3$ action\nto accommodate the \
presence of the scalar field. Second, to establish a\nwell-posed variational \
principle, we extend the renormalized AdS$_3$ action to\ninclude the scalar \
field and incorporate the Gibbons--Hawking--York term for\ninternal \
boundaries and domain wall tension. We engage in holographic\ncomputations, \
thereby determining the explicit form of the holographic stress\ntensor. In \
this context, the stress tensor can be expressed as that of a\nperfect fluid \
situated on a curved background. Additionally, it paves the road\nto \
ascertain the spacetime mass. Finally, we close by demonstrating the\n\
existence of three-dimensional accelerating spacetimes with asymptotically\n\
locally flat and asymptotically locally de Sitter geometries, particularly\n\
those embodying black holes.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 11 Sep 2023 15:47:40 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 13 Nov 2023 21:01:45 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2023-11-15", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Cisterna", "Adolfo", ""}, {
               "Diaz", "Felipe", ""}, {"Mann", "Robert B.", ""}, {
               "Oliva", "Julio", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
