               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2309.07290\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Omkar Shetye\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"R. Loganayagam and Omkar Shetye\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Influence Phase of a dS Observer I : Scalar \
Exchange\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages + 47 pages of appendices. v3: minor improvements\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Inspired by real-time computations in AdS black holes, \
we propose a method to\\nobtain the influence phase of a cosmological \
observer by calculating the\\non-shell action on a doubled spacetime \
geometry. The influence phase is the\\neffective action for an open system: \
for a dS static patch observer coupled to\\na scalar field it incorporates \
the radiation reaction due to the bulk fields\\nand their dS Hawking \
radiation. For a general extended source in dS, we\\ndescribe how to account \
for finite size effects. In the long-time limit, we get\\na Markovian open \
quantum system susceptible to cosmological fluctuations,\\nwhereas the \
short-time limit reproduces the worldline theory of flat-space\\nradiation \
reaction. We also present a fully covariantised form for the \
cubic\\ncorrections to the radiation reaction in even spacetime dimensions, \
including\\nHubble contributions, and find an intriguing recursive structure \
across\\ndimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
