           "id" -> "2309.07290", "submitter" -> "Omkar Shetye", "authors" -> 
            "R. Loganayagam and Omkar Shetye", "title" -> 
            "Influence Phase of a dS Observer I : Scalar Exchange", 
            "comments" -> 
            "22 pages + 47 pages of appendices. v3: minor improvements", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Inspired by real-time computations in AdS black holes, we \
propose a method to\nobtain the influence phase of a cosmological observer by \
calculating the\non-shell action on a doubled spacetime geometry. The \
influence phase is the\neffective action for an open system: for a dS static \
patch observer coupled to\na scalar field it incorporates the radiation \
reaction due to the bulk fields\nand their dS Hawking radiation. For a \
general extended source in dS, we\ndescribe how to account for finite size \
effects. In the long-time limit, we get\na Markovian open quantum system \
susceptible to cosmological fluctuations,\nwhereas the short-time limit \
reproduces the worldline theory of flat-space\nradiation reaction. We also \
present a fully covariantised form for the cubic\ncorrections to the \
radiation reaction in even spacetime dimensions, including\nHubble \
contributions, and find an intriguing recursive structure across\ndimensions.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 13 Sep 2023 20:17:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 25 Sep 2023 15:31:17 GMT"}, {
