 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the OSIRIS-REx mission and ground-based tracking \
data for the asteroid\\nBennu, we derive new constraints on fifth forces and \
ultralight dark matter.\\nThe bounds we obtain are strongest for mediator \
masses $m \\\\sim 10^{-18} -\\n10^{-17}\\\\,{\\\\rm eV}$, where we currently \
achieve the tightest bounds. Our limits\\ncan be translated to a wide class \
of models leading to Yukawa-type fifth\\nforces, and we demonstrate how they \
apply to $U(1)_B$ dark photons and\\nbaryon-coupled scalars. Our results \
demonstrate the potential of asteroid\\ntracking in probing well-motivated \
extensions of the Standard Model and\\nultralight dark matter satisfying the \
fuzzy dark matter constraints.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
