            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2309.14409\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gr\\\\'egoire Mathys\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thomas Hartman and Gr\\\\'egoire Mathys\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Averaged Null Energy and the Renormalization Group\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages including appendices, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We establish a connection between the averaged null \
energy condition (ANEC)\\nand the monotonicity of the renormalization group, \
by studying the light-ray\\noperator $\\\\int du T_{uu}$ in quantum field \
theories that flow between two\\nconformal fixed points. In four dimensions, \
we derive an exact sum rule\\nrelating this operator to the Euler coefficient \
in the trace anomaly, and show\\nthat the ANEC implies the a-theorem. The \
argument is based on matching\\nanomalies in the stress tensor 3-point \
function, and relies on special\\nproperties of contact terms involving \
light-ray operators. We also illustrate\\nthe sum rule for the example of a \
free massive scalar field. Averaged null\\nenergy appears in a variety of \
other applications to quantum field theory,\\nincluding causality \
constraints, Lorentzian inversion, and quantum information.\\nThe quantum \
information perspective provides a new derivation of the\\n$a$-theorem from \
the monotonicity of relative entropy. The equation relating\\nour sum rule to \
the dilaton scattering amplitude in the forward limit suggests\\nan inversion \
formula for non-conformal theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 25 Sep 2023 18:00:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
