            "  We establish a connection between the averaged null energy \
condition (ANEC)\nand the monotonicity of the renormalization group, by \
studying the light-ray\noperator $\\int du T_{uu}$ in quantum field theories \
that flow between two\nconformal fixed points. In four dimensions, we derive \
an exact sum rule\nrelating this operator to the Euler coefficient in the \
trace anomaly, and show\nthat the ANEC implies the a-theorem. The argument is \
based on matching\nanomalies in the stress tensor 3-point function, and \
relies on special\nproperties of contact terms involving light-ray operators. \
We also illustrate\nthe sum rule for the example of a free massive scalar \
field. Averaged null\nenergy appears in a variety of other applications to \
quantum field theory,\nincluding causality constraints, Lorentzian inversion, \
and quantum information.\nThe quantum information perspective provides a new \
derivation of the\n$a$-theorem from the monotonicity of relative entropy. The \
equation relating\nour sum rule to the dilaton scattering amplitude in the \
forward limit suggests\nan inversion formula for non-conformal theories.\n", 
