               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Amitabh Virmani\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Anand Balivada, Pius Ranjan Padhi, Amitabh Virmani\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tidal Forces in Kerr-AdS and Grey Galaxies\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 2 figures; v2: 26 pages, clarifications added, \
CQG version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class. Quantum Grav. 41 125008 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1361-6382/ad494b\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In a recent paper [arXiv:2305.08922], it has been \
proposed that the endpoint\\nof the Kerr-AdS superradiant instability is a \
Grey Galaxy. The conjectured\\nsolutions are supposed to be made up of a \
black hole with critical angular\\nvelocity in the centre of AdS, surrounded \
by a large flat disk of thermal bulk\\ngas that revolves around the black \
hole. In the analysis of the proposed\\nsolutions so far, gravitational \
effects due to the black hole on the thermal\\ngas have been neglected. A way \
to estimate these effects is via computing tidal\\nforces. With this \
motivation, we study tidal forces on objects moving in the\\nKerr-AdS \
spacetime. To do so, we construct a parallel-transported orthonormal\\nframe \
along an arbitrary timelike or null geodesic. We then specialise to \
the\\nclass of fast rotating geodesics lying in the equatorial plane, and \
estimate\\ntidal forces on the gas in the Grey Galaxies, modelling it as a \
collection of\\nparticles moving on timelike geodesics. We show that the \
tidal forces are small\\n(and remain small even in the large mass limit), \
thereby providing additional\\nsupport to the idea that the gas is weakly \
interacting with the black hole.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 26 Sep 2023 04:59:05 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
