                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We provide the analytic waveform in time domain for the \
scattering of two\\nKerr black holes at leading order in the post-Minkowskian \
expansion and up to\\nfourth order in both spins. The result is obtained by \
the generalization of the\\nKMOC formalism to radiative observables, combined \
with the analytic\\ncontinuation of the five-point scattering amplitude to \
complex kinematics. We\\nuse analyticity arguments to express the waveform \
directly in terms of the\\nthree-point coupling of the graviton to the \
spinning particles and the\\ngravitational Compton amplitudes, completely \
bypassing the need to compute and\\nintegrate the five-point amplitude. In \
particular, this allows to easily\\ninclude higher-order spin contributions \
for any spinning compact body. Finally,\\nin the spinless case we find a new \
compact and gauge-invariant representation\\nof the Kovacs-Thorne \
waveform.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
