Gowdy, Gabriele\\n  Travaglini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Resummed spinning waveforms from five-point \
amplitudes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, 6 figures. v3: JHEP version, typos corrected, \
references\\n  added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 02 (2024) 026\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2024)026\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"QMUL-PH-23-18\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th astro-ph.HE gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the classical tree-level five-point \
amplitude for the two-to-two\\nscattering of spinning celestial objects with \
the emission of a graviton. Using\\nthis five-point amplitude, we then turn \
to the computation of the leading-order\\ntime-domain gravitational waveform. \
The method we describe is suitable for\\narbitrary values of classical spin \
of Kerr black holes and does not require any\\nexpansion in powers of the \
spin. In this paper we illustrate it in the simpler\\ncase of the scattering \
of one Kerr and one Schwarzschild black hole. An\\nimportant ingredient of \
our calculation is a novel form of the Compton\\namplitude with spinning \
particles including contact terms derived from matching\\nto black-hole \
perturbation theory calculations. This ensures that our waveform\\nis valid \
up to at least fourth order in the spin. Our method can be \
applied\\nimmediately to generate improved waveforms once higher-order \
contact terms in\\nthe Compton amplitude become available. Finally, we show \
the formula for the\\ngravitational memory to all orders in the spin, which \
is in agreement with our\\nresults.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
