           "id" -> "2310.09839", "submitter" -> "Keisuke Nakashi", "authors" -> 
            "Keisuke Nakashi, Masashi Kimura, Hayato Motohashi, Kazufumi \
Takahashi", "title" -> 
            "Black hole ringdown from physically sensible initial value \
problem in\n  higher-order scalar-tensor theories", "comments" -> 
            "36 pages, 11 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D109, no.2, 024034 (2024)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.109.024034", "report-no" -> 
            "RUP-23-19, YITP-23-118", "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study odd-parity perturbations about static and spherically \
symmetric\nblack hole solutions with a linearly time-dependent scalar field \
in\nhigher-order scalar-tensor theories. In particular, we consider stealth\n\
Schwarzschild and stealth Schwarzschild-de Sitter solutions, where the\n\
deviation from the general relativity case is controlled by a single \
parameter.\nWe find that complex frequencies of quasinormal modes (QNMs) are \
given by a\nsimple scaling of those in general relativity. We also show that \
there is a\ndegeneracy between the parameter characterizing the modification \
from general\nrelativity and the black hole mass. We then consider a \
physically sensible\ninitial value problem by taking into account the fact \
that the effective metric\nfor the odd-parity perturbations is in general \
different from the background\nmetric. We confirm that damped oscillations \
appearing at late times are indeed\ndominated by the QNMs. Our analysis \
includes the case where the perturbations\nare superluminal, and we \
demonstrate in this case that the perturbations can\nescape from the region \
inside the horizon for the background metric.\n", 
