bi-Lanczos algorithm, which\ntransforms the Lindbladian into a pure \
tridiagonal form. We find that the\nKrylov complexity saturates inversely \
with the dissipation strength, while the\ndissipative timescale grows \
logarithmically. This is akin to the behavior of\nother \
$\\mathfrak{q}$-complexity measures, namely out-of-time-order correlator\n\
(OTOC) and operator size, which we also demonstrate. We connect these\n\
observations to continuous quantum measurement processes. We further\n\
investigate the pole structure of a generic auto-correlation and the\n\
high-frequency behavior of the spectral function in the presence of\n\
dissipation, thereby revealing a general principle for operator growth in\n\
dissipative quantum chaotic systems.\n", 
