                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the renormalization of a particular sector of \
Horndeski theory. In\\nparticular, we focus on the nonminimal coupling of a \
scalar field to the\\nGauss-Bonnet term and its kinetic coupling to the \
Einstein tensor. Adopting a\\npower expansion on the scalar function that \
couples the Gauss-Bonnet term, we\\nfind specific conditions on their \
coefficients such that the action and charges\\nare finite. To accomplish the \
latter, we add a finite set of intrinsic boundary\\nterms. The contribution \
of the nonminimal coupling generates an effective\\nscalar mass, allowing us \
to recover a modified Breitenlohner-Freedman bound.\\nFurthermore, we compute \
the holographic 1-point functions and Ward identities\\nassociated with the \
scalar field and the metric. We constrain the parameter\\nspace of the theory \
by taking into account the preservation of scaling symmetry\\nat the \
boundary.\\n\""}]}, {
