                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Superradiance is the effect of field waves being \
amplified during reflection\\nfrom a charged or rotating black hole. In this \
paper, we study the low-energy\\ndynamics of super-radiant scattering of \
massive scalar and massless higher spin\\nfield perturbations in a generic \
axisymmetric stationary Kerr-Taub-NUT\\n(Newman-Unti-Tamburino) spacetime, \
which represents sources with both\\ngravitomagnetic monopole moment \
(magnetic mass) and gravitomagnetic dipole\\nmoment (angular momentum). We \
obtain a generalized Teukolsky master equation\\nfor all spin perturbation \
fields. The equations are separated into their\\nangular and radial parts. \
The angular equations lead to spin-weighted\\nspheroidal harmonic functions \
that generalize those in Kerr spacetime. We\\nidentify an effective spin as a \
coupling between frequency (or energy) and the\\nNUT parameter. The behaviors \
of the radial wave function near the horizon and\\nat the infinite boundary \
are studied. We provide analytical expressions for\\nlow-energy observables \
such as emission rates and cross sections of all\\nmassless fields with spin, \
including scalar, neutrino, electromagnetic,\\nRarita-Schwinger, and \
gravitational waves.\\n\""}]}, {
