                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Extraction of multiple quasinormal modes from ringdown \
gravitational waves\\nemitted from a binary black hole coalescence is a \
touchstone to test whether a\\nremnant black hole is described by the Kerr \
spacetime in general relativity.\\nHowever, it is not straightforward to \
check the consistency between the\\nringdown signal and the quasinormal mode \
frequencies predicted by the linear\\nperturbation theory. While the \
longest-lived mode can be extracted in a stable\\nmanner, the higher \
overtones damp more quickly and hence the fitting of\\novertones tends to end \
up with the overfit. To improve the extraction of\\novertones, we propose an \
iterative procedure consisting of fitting and\\nsubtraction of the \
longest-lived mode of the ringdown waveform in the time\\ndomain. Through the \
analyses of the mock waveform and numerical relativity\\nwaveform, we clarify \
that the iterative procedure allows us to extract the\\novertones in a more \
stable manner.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
