Cardoso\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ringdown of a dynamical spacetime\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"17 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 109, 044048 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.109.044048\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"gr-qc astro-ph.HE hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The gravitational waves emitted (some time) after two \
black holes merge are\\nwell described by the theory of linear perturbations \
on a spacetime\\ncharacterized by the mass and spin of the remnant. However, \
in the very early\\nstages right after merger, both the mass and spin are \
changing. In this work we\\nexplore, in a set up based on Vaidya's spacetime, \
the dynamical consequences of\\na change of mass in the spacetime due to the \
accretion of null matter (for\\nexample, gravitational waves). We show that \
accretion imprints time-dependent\\nfrequencies and amplitude to a ringdown \
waveform, and we show how to model\\naccurately this effect in certain \
regimes. We also comment on the direct\\nemission of gravitational waves due \
to perturbations in the in--falling matter,\\nwhich is of relevance for black \
holes embedded in astrophysical environments.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
