very early\nstages right after merger, both the mass and spin are changing. \
In this work we\nexplore, in a set up based on Vaidya's spacetime, the \
dynamical consequences of\na change of mass in the spacetime due to the \
accretion of null matter (for\nexample, gravitational waves). We show that \
accretion imprints time-dependent\nfrequencies and amplitude to a ringdown \
waveform, and we show how to model\naccurately this effect in certain \
regimes. We also comment on the direct\nemission of gravitational waves due \
to perturbations in the in--falling matter,\nwhich is of relevance for black \
holes embedded in astrophysical environments.\n", 
