               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We set up the Kosower, Maybee, O'Connell formalism for \
generic spin following\\na previous field theory construction and use it to \
extract a next-to-leading\\norder eikonal formula for the linear-in-spin \
momentum impulse, $\\\\Delta\\np^{\\\\mu}$, and spin kick, $\\\\Delta \
S^{\\\\mu \\\\nu}$. We explicitly test the formalism\\nfor the case of \
electrodynamics and find agreement with previous QFT and\\nworldline results. \
This includes the case where multiple spins propagate with\\nallowed spin \
transitions, or equivalently where no spin supplementary condition\\nis \
imposed on the worldline equations of motion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
