and Filippo\\n  Vernizzi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Vanishing of Nonlinear Tidal Love Numbers of \
Schwarzschild Black Holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"11 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is well known that asymptotically flat Schwarzschild \
black holes in\\ngeneral relativity in four spacetime dimensions have \
vanishing induced linear\\ntidal response. We extend this result beyond \
linear order for the polar sector,\\nby solving the static nonlinear Einstein \
equations for the perturbations of the\\nSchwarzschild metric and computing \
the quadratic corrections to the\\nelectric-type tidal Love numbers. After \
explicitly performing the matching with\\nthe point-particle effective theory \
at leading order in the derivative\\nexpansion, we show that the Love number \
couplings remain zero at higher order\\nin perturbation theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
