Filippo\n  Vernizzi", "title" -> 
            "Vanishing of Nonlinear Tidal Love Numbers of Schwarzschild Black \
Holes", "comments" -> "11 pages, 3 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  It is well known that asymptotically flat Schwarzschild black \
holes in\ngeneral relativity in four spacetime dimensions have vanishing \
induced linear\ntidal response. We extend this result beyond linear order for \
the polar sector,\nby solving the static nonlinear Einstein equations for the \
perturbations of the\nSchwarzschild metric and computing the quadratic \
corrections to the\nelectric-type tidal Love numbers. After explicitly \
performing the matching with\nthe point-particle effective theory at leading \
order in the derivative\nexpansion, we show that the Love number couplings \
remain zero at higher order\nin perturbation theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
