                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2312.05965\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Zihan Zhou\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Yilber Fabian Bautista, Giulio Bonelli, Cristoforo \
Iossa, Alessandro\\n  Tanzini, Zihan Zhou\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Black Hole Perturbation Theory Meets CFT$_2$: Kerr \
Compton Amplitudes\\n  from Nekrasov-Shatashvili Functions\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"18 pages, 3 figs; the helicity reversing amplitude is \
considered in\\n  the new version\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc hep-ph\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We present a novel study of Kerr Compton amplitudes in \
a partial wave basis\\nin terms of the Nekrasov-Shatashvili (NS) function of \
the confluent Heun\\nequation (CHE). Remarkably, NS-functions enjoy analytic \
properties and\\nsymmetries that are naturally inherited by the Compton \
amplitudes. Based on\\nthis, we characterize the analytic dependence of the \
Compton phase-shift in the\\nKerr spin parameter and provide a direct \
comparison to the standard\\npost-Minkowskian (PM) perturbative approach \
within General Relativity (GR). We\\nalso analyze the universal large \
frequency behavior of the relevant\\ncharacteristic exponent of the CHE -- \
also known as the renormalized angular\\nmomentum -- and find agreement with \
numerical computations. Moreover, we\\ndiscuss the analytic continuation in \
the harmonics quantum number $\\\\ell$ of the\\npartial wave, and show that \
the limit to the physical integer values commutes\\nwith the PM expansion of \
the observables. Finally, we obtain the contributions\\nto the tree level, \
point-particle, gravitational Compton amplitude in a\\ncovariant basis \
through $O(a_{\\\\text{BH}}^8)$, without the need to take \
the\\nsuper-extremal limit for Kerr spin.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 10 Dec 2023 18:44:29 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 30 Jul 2024 23:00:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                    "}"}]}]}, {
