               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2312.07452\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Carlo Heissenberg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alessandro Georgoudis, Carlo Heissenberg, Rodolfo \
Russo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"An eikonal-inspired approach to the gravitational \
scattering waveform\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, v2: presentation improved\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"QMUL-PH-23-34\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the amplitude-based derivation of \
gravitational waveform for the\\nscattering of two scalar black holes at \
subleading post-Minkowskian (PM) order.\\nWe take an eikonal-inspired \
approach to the two-massive-particle cut needed in\\nthe KMOC framework, as \
highlighted in arXiv:2308.02125, and show that its\\neffect is to implement a \
simple change of frame. This clarifies one of the\\npoints raised in \
arXiv:2309.14925 when comparing with the post-Newtonian (PN)\\nresults. We \
then provide an explicit PM expression for the waveform in the soft\\nlimit, \
$\\\\omega\\\\to0$, including the first non-universal, \
$\\\\omega\\\\log\\\\omega$,\\ncontribution. Focusing on this regime, we show \
that the small-velocity limit of\\nour result agrees with the soft limit of \
the PN waveform of arXiv:2309.14925,\\nprovided that the two quantities are \
written in the same asymptotic frame.\\nPerforming the BMS supertranslation \
that, as discussed in arXiv:2201.11607, is\\nresponsible for the $\\\\mathcal \
O(G)$ static contribution to the asymptotic field\\nemployed in the PN \
literature, we find agreement between the amplitude-based\\nand the PN soft \
waveform up to and including $G^3/c^5$ order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
