           "id" -> "2312.07452", "submitter" -> "Carlo Heissenberg", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Alessandro Georgoudis, Carlo Heissenberg, Rodolfo Russo", 
            "title" -> 
            "An eikonal-inspired approach to the gravitational scattering \
waveform", "comments" -> "40 pages, v2: presentation improved", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "QMUL-PH-23-34", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the amplitude-based derivation of gravitational \
waveform for the\nscattering of two scalar black holes at subleading \
post-Minkowskian (PM) order.\nWe take an eikonal-inspired approach to the \
two-massive-particle cut needed in\nthe KMOC framework, as highlighted in \
arXiv:2308.02125, and show that its\neffect is to implement a simple change \
of frame. This clarifies one of the\npoints raised in arXiv:2309.14925 when \
comparing with the post-Newtonian (PN)\nresults. We then provide an explicit \
PM expression for the waveform in the soft\nlimit, $\\omega\\to0$, including \
the first non-universal, $\\omega\\log\\omega$,\ncontribution. Focusing on \
this regime, we show that the small-velocity limit of\nour result agrees with \
the soft limit of the PN waveform of arXiv:2309.14925,\nprovided that the two \
quantities are written in the same asymptotic frame.\nPerforming the BMS \
supertranslation that, as discussed in arXiv:2201.11607, is\nresponsible for \
the $\\mathcal O(G)$ static contribution to the asymptotic field\nemployed in \
the PN literature, we find agreement between the amplitude-based\nand the PN \
soft waveform up to and including $G^3/c^5$ order.\n", 
