                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study CFTs at finite temperature and derive explicit \
sum rules for\\none-point functions of operators by imposing the KMS \
condition. In the case of\\na large gap between light and heavy operators, we \
explicitly compute one-point\\nfunctions for light operators. Turning to \
heavy operators we employ Tauberian\\ntheorems and compute the asymptotic OPE \
density for heavy operators, from which\\nwe extract the leading terms of the \
OPE coefficients associated with heavy\\noperators. Furthermore, we \
approximate and establish bounds for the two-point\\nfunctions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
