 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We employ a deep learning method to deduce the \
\\\\textit{bulk} spacetime from\\n\\\\textit{boundary} optical conductivity. \
We apply the neural ordinary\\ndifferential equation technique, tailored for \
continuous functions such as the\\nmetric, to the typical class of \
holographic condensed matter models featuring\\nbroken translations: \
linear-axion models. We successfully extract the bulk\\nmetric from the \
boundary holographic optical conductivity. Furthermore, as an\\nexample for \
real material, we use experimental optical conductivity of\\n$\\\\text{UPd}_2\
\\\\text{Al}_3$, a representative of heavy fermion metals in \
strongly\\ncorrelated electron systems, and construct the corresponding bulk \
metric. To\\nour knowledge, our work is the first illustration of deep \
learning bulk\\nspacetime from \\\\textit{boundary} holographic or \
experimental conductivity data.\\n\""}]}, {
