               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Next-to-eikonal corrected double graviton dressing and \
gravitational\\n  wave observables at ${\\\\cal O}(G^2)$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matches published version; 49 pages, 1 figure, revisions \
of Sec. 2.3,\\n  Sec. 4.1 and Sec. 5 with broader literature review, minor \
revision of\\n  notation and typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Following a recent proposal to describe inelastic \
eikonal scattering\\nprocesses in terms of gravitationally dressed elastic \
eikonal amplitudes, we\\nmotivate a collinear double graviton dressing and \
investigate its properties.\\nThis is derived from a generalized Wilson line \
operator in the worldline\\nformalism by integrating over fluctuations of the \
eikonal trajectories of\\nexternal particles in gravitationally interacting \
theories. The dressing can be\\nexpressed as a product of exponential terms \
-- a coherent piece with\\ncontributions to all odd orders in the \
gravitational coupling constant and a\\nterm quadratic in graviton modes, \
with the former providing classical\\ngravitational wave observables. In \
particular, the coherent dressing involves\\n$\\\\mathcal{O}(\\\\kappa^3)$ \
subleading double graviton corrections to the Weinberg\\nsoft factor. We use \
this dressing to derive expressions for the waveform,\\nradiative momentum \
spectrum and angular momentum. In a limiting case of the\\nwaveform, we \
derive the nonlinear memory effect resulting from the emission of\\nnearly \
soft gravitons from a scattering process.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
