            "  Following a recent proposal to describe inelastic eikonal \
scattering\nprocesses in terms of gravitationally dressed elastic eikonal \
amplitudes, we\nmotivate a collinear double graviton dressing and investigate \
its properties.\nThis is derived from a generalized Wilson line operator in \
the worldline\nformalism by integrating over fluctuations of the eikonal \
trajectories of\nexternal particles in gravitationally interacting theories. \
The dressing can be\nexpressed as a product of exponential terms -- a \
coherent piece with\ncontributions to all odd orders in the gravitational \
coupling constant and a\nterm quadratic in graviton modes, with the former \
providing classical\ngravitational wave observables. In particular, the \
coherent dressing involves\n$\\mathcal{O}(\\kappa^3)$ subleading double \
graviton corrections to the Weinberg\nsoft factor. We use this dressing to \
derive expressions for the waveform,\nradiative momentum spectrum and angular \
momentum. In a limiting case of the\nwaveform, we derive the nonlinear memory \
effect resulting from the emission of\nnearly soft gravitons from a \
scattering process.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
