            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We conjecture a set of differential equations that \
characterizes the\nLiouville irregular states of half-integer ranks, which \
extends the generalized\nAGT correspondence to all the $(A_1,A_\\text{even})$ \
and $(A_1,D_\\text{odd})$\ntypes Argyres-Douglas theories. For lower \
half-integer ranks, our conjecture is\nverified by deriving it as a suitable \
limit of a similar set of differential\nequations for integer ranks. This \
limit is interpreted as the 2D counterpart of\na 4D RG-flow from \
$(A_1,D_{2n})$ to $(A_1,D_{2n-1})$. For rank $3/2$, we solve\nthe conjectured \
differential equations and find a power series expression for\nthe irregular \
state $|I^{(3/2)}\\rangle$. For rank $5/2$, our conjecture is\nconsistent \
with the differential equations recently discovered by H. Poghosyan\nand R. \
Poghossian.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 26 Jan 2024 05:57:56 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
