               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sergio Cacciatori\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sergio L. Cacciatori, Fabrizio Canfora, Federica \
Muscolino\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pearcey integrals, Stokes lines and exact baryonic layers \
in the low\\n  energy limit of QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph nucl-th\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The first analytic solutions representing baryonic \
layers living at finite\\nbaryon density within a constant magnetic field in \
the gauged Skyrme model are\\nconstructed. A remarkable feature of these \
configurations is that, if the\\nSkyrme term is neglected, then these \
baryonic layers in the constant magnetic\\nbackground cannot be found \
analytically and their energies grow very fast with\\nthe magnetic field. On \
the other hand, if the Skyrme term is taken into\\naccount, the field \
equations can be solved analytically and the corresponding\\nsolutions have a \
smooth limit for large magnetic fields. Thus, the Skyrme term\\ndiscloses the \
universal character of these configurations living at finite\\nBaryon density \
in a constant magnetic field. The classical gran-canonical\\npartition \
function of these configurations can be expressed explicitly in terms\\nof \
the Pearcey integral. This fact allows us to determine analytically \
the\\nStokes lines of the partition function and the corresponding dependence \
on the\\nbaryonic chemical potential as well as on the external magnetic \
field. In this\\nway, we can determine various critical curves in the \
($\\\\mu_B-B_{ext}$) plane\\nwhich separates different physical behaviors. \
These families of inhomogeneous\\nbaryonic condensates can be also dressed \
with chiral conformal excitations of\\nthe solutions representing modulations \
of the layers themselves. Some physical\\nconsequences are \
analyzed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
