            "title" -> 
            "Pearcey integrals, Stokes lines and exact baryonic layers in the \
low\n  energy limit of QCD", "comments" -> "31 pages, 8 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph nucl-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The first analytic solutions representing baryonic layers \
living at finite\nbaryon density within a constant magnetic field in the \
gauged Skyrme model are\nconstructed. A remarkable feature of these \
configurations is that, if the\nSkyrme term is neglected, then these baryonic \
layers in the constant magnetic\nbackground cannot be found analytically and \
their energies grow very fast with\nthe magnetic field. On the other hand, if \
the Skyrme term is taken into\naccount, the field equations can be solved \
analytically and the corresponding\nsolutions have a smooth limit for large \
magnetic fields. Thus, the Skyrme term\ndiscloses the universal character of \
these configurations living at finite\nBaryon density in a constant magnetic \
field. The classical gran-canonical\npartition function of these \
configurations can be expressed explicitly in terms\nof the Pearcey integral. \
This fact allows us to determine analytically the\nStokes lines of the \
partition function and the corresponding dependence on the\nbaryonic chemical \
potential as well as on the external magnetic field. In this\nway, we can \
determine various critical curves in the ($\\mu_B-B_{ext}$) plane\nwhich \
separates different physical behaviors. These families of inhomogeneous\n\
baryonic condensates can be also dressed with chiral conformal excitations of\
\nthe solutions representing modulations of the layers themselves. Some \
physical\nconsequences are analyzed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
