Dorin Weissman\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"From spectral to scattering form factor\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"47 pages, 17 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITCP-IPP-2024/3\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.CD\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a novel indicator for chaotic quantum \
scattering processes, the\\nscattering form factor (ScFF). It is based on \
mapping the locations of peaks in\\nthe scattering amplitude to random matrix \
eigenvalues, and computing the analog\\nof the spectral form factor (SFF). We \
compute the spectral and scattering form\\nfactors of several non-chaotic \
systems. We determine the ScFF associated with\\nthe phase shifts of the \
leaky torus, closely related to the distribution of the\\nzeros of Riemann \
zeta function. We compute the ScFF for the decay amplitude of\\na highly \
excited string states into two tachyons. We show that it displays \
the\\nuniversal features expected from random matrix theory - a decline, a \
ramp and a\\nplateau - and is in general agreement with the Gaussian unitary \
ensemble. It\\nalso shows some new features, owning to the special structure \
of the string\\namplitude, including a \\\"bump\\\" before the ramp \
associated with gaps in the\\naverage eigenvalue density. The \\\"bump\\\" is \
removed for highly excited string\\nstates with an appropriate state \
dependent unfolding. We also discuss the SFF\\nfor the Gaussian $\\\\beta$- \
ensemble, writing an interpolation between the known\\nresults of the \
Gaussian orthogonal, unitary, and symplectic ensembles.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 1 Mar 2024 17:54:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 23 Apr 2024 16:47:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
