         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2403.00713", "submitter" -> "Maurizio Firrotta", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Massimo Bianchi, Maurizio Firrotta, Jacob Sonnenschein, Dorin \
Weissman", "title" -> "From spectral to scattering form factor", "comments" -> 
            "47 pages, 17 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "ITCP-IPP-2024/3", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th nlin.CD", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose a novel indicator for chaotic quantum scattering \
processes, the\nscattering form factor (ScFF). It is based on mapping the \
locations of peaks in\nthe scattering amplitude to random matrix eigenvalues, \
and computing the analog\nof the spectral form factor (SFF). We compute the \
spectral and scattering form\nfactors of several non-chaotic systems. We \
determine the ScFF associated with\nthe phase shifts of the leaky torus, \
closely related to the distribution of the\nzeros of Riemann zeta function. \
We compute the ScFF for the decay amplitude of\na highly excited string \
states into two tachyons. We show that it displays the\nuniversal features \
expected from random matrix theory - a decline, a ramp and a\nplateau - and \
is in general agreement with the Gaussian unitary ensemble. It\nalso shows \
some new features, owning to the special structure of the string\namplitude, \
including a \"bump\" before the ramp associated with gaps in the\naverage \
eigenvalue density. The \"bump\" is removed for highly excited string\nstates \
with an appropriate state dependent unfolding. We also discuss the SFF\nfor \
the Gaussian $\\beta$- ensemble, writing an interpolation between the known\n\
results of the Gaussian orthogonal, unitary, and symplectic ensembles.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 1 Mar 2024 17:54:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 23 Apr 2024 16:47:02 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-04-24", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bianchi", "Massimo", ""}, {
              "Firrotta", "Maurizio", ""}, {"Sonnenschein", "Jacob", ""}, {
              "Weissman", "Dorin", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
