               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning Particle Geometries in AdS$_3$/CFT$_2$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 1 figure; comments welcome! v2: 26 pages, 2 \
figures,\\n  improved various discussions, added references, corrected minor \
typos v3:\\n  clarifications regarding boundary conditions added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2024)216\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study spinning particle/defect geometries in the \
context of\\nAdS$_3$/CFT$_2$. These solutions lie below the BTZ threshold, \
and can be\\nobtained from identifications of AdS$_3$. We construct the \
Feynman propagator\\nby solving the bulk equation of motion in the spinning \
particle geometry,\\nsumming over the modes of the fields and passing to the \
boundary. The\\nquantization of the scalar fields becomes challenging when \
confined to the\\nregions that are causally well-behaved. If the region \
containing closed\\ntimelike curves (CTCs) is included, the normalization of \
the scalar fields\\nenjoys an analytical simplification and the propagator \
can be expressed as an\\ninfinite sum over image geodesics. In the dual \
CFT$_2$, the propagator can be\\nrecast as the HHLL four-point function, \
where by taking into account the $PSL\\n(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ modular images, we \
recover the bulk computation. We comment on\\nthe casual behavior of bulk \
geometries associated with single-trace operators\\nof spin scaling with the \
central charge below the BTZ threshold.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
