            "Ziyi Li", "title" -> 
            "Spinning Particle Geometries in AdS$_3$/CFT$_2$", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages, 1 figure; comments welcome! v2: 26 pages, 2 figures,\n \
 improved various discussions, added references, corrected minor typos v3:\n  \
clarifications regarding boundary conditions added", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2024)216", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study spinning particle/defect geometries in the context of\
\nAdS$_3$/CFT$_2$. These solutions lie below the BTZ threshold, and can be\n\
obtained from identifications of AdS$_3$. We construct the Feynman propagator\
\nby solving the bulk equation of motion in the spinning particle geometry,\n\
summing over the modes of the fields and passing to the boundary. The\n\
quantization of the scalar fields becomes challenging when confined to the\n\
regions that are causally well-behaved. If the region containing closed\n\
timelike curves (CTCs) is included, the normalization of the scalar fields\n\
enjoys an analytical simplification and the propagator can be expressed as an\
\ninfinite sum over image geodesics. In the dual CFT$_2$, the propagator can \
be\nrecast as the HHLL four-point function, where by taking into account the \
$PSL\n(2,\\mathbb{Z})$ modular images, we recover the bulk computation. We \
comment on\nthe casual behavior of bulk geometries associated with \
single-trace operators\nof spin scaling with the central charge below the BTZ \
threshold.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 8 Mar 2024 18:44:57 GMT"}, {
