        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{5.331466671017844, 5.566040015951949}, 0.08283829248930569],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2403.06006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yuk Ting Albert Law\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Manvir Grewal, Y.T. Albert Law\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Real-time observables in de Sitter thermodynamics\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31+10 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study real-time finite-temperature correlators for \
free scalars of any\\nmass in a $dS_{d+1}$ static patch in any dimension. We \
show that whenever the\\ninverse temperature is a rational multiple of the \
inverse de Sitter\\ntemperature, certain Matsubara poles of the symmetric \
Wightman function\\ndisappear. At the de Sitter temperature, we explicitly \
show how the Lorentzian\\nthermal correlators can all be obtained by analytic \
continuations from the\\nround $S^{d+1}$. We establish the precise relation \
between the Harish-Chandra\\ncharacter for $SO(1,d+1)$ and the integrated \
spectral function, providing a\\nnovel dynamical perspective on the former \
and enabling generalizations.\\nFurthermore, we study scalars with \
exceptional non-positive masses. We provide\\na physical picture for the \
distinctive structures of their characters. For the\\nmassless case, we \
perform a consistent static patch quantization, and find the\\nunique \
$S^{d+1}$ correlator that analytically continues to the correlators in\\nthe \
quantum theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 9 Mar 2024 20:59:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-03-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
