         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2403.06006", "submitter" -> "Yuk Ting Albert Law", 
            "authors" -> "Manvir Grewal, Y.T. Albert Law", "title" -> 
            "Real-time observables in de Sitter thermodynamics", "comments" -> 
            "31+10 pages, 8 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study real-time finite-temperature correlators for free \
scalars of any\nmass in a $dS_{d+1}$ static patch in any dimension. We show \
that whenever the\ninverse temperature is a rational multiple of the inverse \
de Sitter\ntemperature, certain Matsubara poles of the symmetric Wightman \
function\ndisappear. At the de Sitter temperature, we explicitly show how the \
Lorentzian\nthermal correlators can all be obtained by analytic continuations \
from the\nround $S^{d+1}$. We establish the precise relation between the \
Harish-Chandra\ncharacter for $SO(1,d+1)$ and the integrated spectral \
function, providing a\nnovel dynamical perspective on the former and enabling \
generalizations.\nFurthermore, we study scalars with exceptional non-positive \
masses. We provide\na physical picture for the distinctive structures of \
their characters. For the\nmassless case, we perform a consistent static \
patch quantization, and find the\nunique $S^{d+1}$ correlator that \
analytically continues to the correlators in\nthe quantum theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 9 Mar 2024 20:59:57 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-03-12", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Grewal", "Manvir", ""}, {
              "Law", "Y. T. Albert", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{0.053900403183352985`, 4.834241094727565}, 
           0.08283829248930569],
