                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sheng Long, Weike Deng, Jiliang Jing\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Energy flux and waveforms by coalescing spinless binary \
system in\\n  effective one-body theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"33 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SCIENCE CHINA Physics, Mechanics & Astronomy, 2024, V67, \
260412\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s11433-023-2354-1\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a study on the energy radiation rate and \
waveforms of the\\ngravitational wave generated by coalescing spinless binary \
systems up to the\\nthird post-Minkowskian approximation in the effective \
one-body theory. To\\nderive an analytical expansion of the null tetrad \
components of the\\ngravitational perturbed Weyl tensor $\\\\varPsi_{4}$ in \
the effective spacetime,\\nwe utilize the method proposed by Sasaki $et$ \
$al.$ During this investigation,\\nwe discover more general integral formulas \
that provide a theoretical framework\\nfor computing the results in any \
order. Subsequently, we successfully compute\\nthe energy radiation rate and \
waveforms of the gravitational wave, which\\ninclude the results of the \
Schwarzschild case and the correction terms\\nresulting from the \
dimensionless parameters $a_{2}$ and $a_{3}$ in the\\neffective \
metric.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
