          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2403.10605\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dimitrios Giataganas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"D. Giataganas, A. Kehagias, A. Riotto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quasinormal Modes and Universality of the Penrose Limit \
of Black Hole\\n  Photon Rings\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"33 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"gr-qc astro-ph.CO astro-ph.HE hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the physics of photon rings in a wide range of \
axisymmetric black\\nholes admitting a separable Hamilton-Jacobi equation for \
the geodesics.\\nUtilizing the Killing-Yano tensor, we derive the Penrose \
limit of the black\\nholes, which describes the physics near the photon ring. \
The obtained plane\\nwave geometry is directly linked to the frequency matrix \
of the massless wave\\nequation, as well as the instabilities and Lyapunov \
exponents of the null\\ngeodesics. Consequently, the Lyapunov exponents and \
frequencies of the photon\\ngeodesics, along with the quasinormal modes, can \
be all extracted from a\\nHamiltonian in the Penrose limit plane wave metric. \
Additionally, we explore\\npotential bounds on the Lyapunov exponent, the \
orbital and precession\\nfrequencies, in connection with the corresponding \
inverted harmonic oscillators\\nand we discuss the possibility of photon \
rings serving as holographic horizons\\nin a holographic duality framework \
for astrophysical black holes. Our formalism\\nis applicable to spacetimes \
encompassing various types of black holes,\\nincluding stationary ones like \
Kerr, Kerr-Newman, as well as static black holes\\nsuch as Schwarzschild, \
Reissner-Nordstr\\\\\\\"om, among others.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 15 Mar 2024 18:00:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-03-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Giataganas\"", ",", "\"D.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kehagias\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Riotto\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
