               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Naotaka Kubo and Tomoki Nosaka\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Fermi gas formalism for D-type quiver Chern-Simons theory \
with\\n  non-uniform ranks\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"47 pages, 11 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the Fermi gas formalism for the partition \
function of\\nsupersymmetric Chern-Simons theories with affine $D$-type \
quiver diagrams with\\nnon-uniform ranks of the gauge groups and \
Fayet-Illiopoulos parameters by two\\ndifferent approaches: the open string \
formalism and the closed string\\nformalism. In the closed string formalism \
approach, we find a novel connection\\nbetween the partition function of this \
theory and the partition function of a\\nfour-nodes circular quiver \
supersymmetric Chern-Simons theory. We also studied\\na symmetry of a density \
matrix appeared in the closed string formalism. We\\nfurther calculate the \
exact values of the partition function for finite $N$,\\nwith which we \
identified the exponent of the leading non-perturbative effect in\\n$1/N$ \
corresponding to the worldsheet instantons in the circular \
quiver\\nsupersymmetric Chern-Simons theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
