            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the gravitational anomaly vertex $\\langle \
TTJ_5\\rangle$\n(graviton - graviton - axial current) under conditions of \
finite density and\ntemperature. Through a direct analysis of perturbative \
contributions, we\ndemonstrate that neither finite temperature nor finite \
fermion density affects\nthe gravitational chiral anomaly. These results find \
application in several\ncontexts, from topological materials to the early \
universe plasma. They affect\nthe decay of any axion or axion-like particle \
into gravitational waves, in very\ndense and hot environments.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 9 Apr 2024 12:47:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-04-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Corian\[OGrave]", "Claudio", ""}, {
              "Cret\[IGrave]", "Mario", ""}, {"Lionetti", "Stefano", ""}, {
              "Tommasi", "Riccardo", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
