            "id" -> "2404.06544", "submitter" -> "Mudit Rai", "authors" -> 
             "Mudit Rai and Luca Santoni", "title" -> 
             
             "Ladder Symmetries and Love Numbers of Reissner--Nordstr\\\"om \
Black Holes", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP07(2024)098", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
             "  It is well known that asymptotically flat black holes in \
general relativity\nhave vanishing tidal Love numbers. In the case of \
Schwarzschild and Kerr black\nholes, this property has been shown to be a \
consequence of a hidden structure\nof ladder symmetries for the \
perturbations. In this work, we extend the ladder\nsymmetries to non-rotating \
charged black holes in general relativity. As\nopposed to previous works in \
this context, we adopt a more general definition\nof Love numbers, including \
quadratic operators that mix gravitational and\nelectromagnetic perturbations \
in the point-particle effective field theory. We\nshow that the calculation \
of a subset of those couplings in full general\nrelativity is affected by an \
ambiguity in the split between source and\nresponse, which we resolve through \
an analytic continuation. As a result, we\nderive a novel master equation \
that unifies scalar, electromagnetic and\ngravitational perturbations around \
Reissner--Nordstr\\\"om black holes. The\nequation is hypergeometric and can \
be obtained from previous formulations via\nnontrivial field redefinitions, \
which allow to systematically remove some of\nthe singularities and make the \
presence of the ladder symmetries more manifest.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
