               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"David Kubiznak, Otakar Sv\\\\'itek, Tayebeh \
Tahamtan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Regularized Conformal Electrodynamics: Novel C-metric in \
(2+1)\\n  Dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Conformal electrodynamics is a particularly interesting \
example of power\\nMaxwell non-linear electrodynamics, designed to possess \
conformal symmetry in\\nall dimensions. In this paper, we propose a \
regularized version of Conformal\\nelectrodynamics, minimally regularizing \
the field of a point charge at the\\norigin by breaking the conformal \
invariance of the theory with a dimensionfull\\n\\\"Born-Infeld-like\\\" \
parameter. In four dimensions the new theory reduces to the\\nrecently \
studied Regularized Maxwell electrodynamics, distinguished by \
its\\n\\\"Maxwell-like\\\" solutions for accelerated and slowly rotating \
black hole\\nspacetimes. Focusing on three dimensions, we show that the new \
theory shares\\nmany of the properties of its four-dimensional cousin, \
including the existence\\nof the charged C-metric solution (currently unknown \
in the Maxwell theory).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
