            "  Conformal electrodynamics is a particularly interesting \
example of power\nMaxwell non-linear electrodynamics, designed to possess \
conformal symmetry in\nall dimensions. In this paper, we propose a \
regularized version of Conformal\nelectrodynamics, minimally regularizing the \
field of a point charge at the\norigin by breaking the conformal invariance \
of the theory with a dimensionfull\n\"Born-Infeld-like\" parameter. In four \
dimensions the new theory reduces to the\nrecently studied Regularized \
Maxwell electrodynamics, distinguished by its\n\"Maxwell-like\" solutions for \
accelerated and slowly rotating black hole\nspacetimes. Focusing on three \
dimensions, we show that the new theory shares\nmany of the properties of its \
four-dimensional cousin, including the existence\nof the charged C-metric \
solution (currently unknown in the Maxwell theory).\n", 
