          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.02328\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Prabwal Phukon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bidyut Hazarika and Prabwal Phukon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Topology of restricted phase space thermodynamics in \
Kerr-Sen-Ads black\\n  holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 pages, 51 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this study, we investigate the thermodynamic \
topology of the Kerr-Sen-Ads\\nblack hole in restricted phase space. In the \
restricted phase space, a new\\nparameter, central charge $C$, and its \
conjugate parameter $\\\\mu$ are\\nintroduced, omitting the well-known $PdV$ \
term in the first law of black hole\\nthermodynamics. We study the local and \
global topology of the black hole by\\nconsidering the black hole solution as \
topological defects in the free energy\\nlandscape. We compute the winding \
number and the total topological number at\\nthe thermodynamic defects. For \
our analysis, we have considered five ensembles\\nof Kerr-Sen-Ads black holes \
in restricted phase space: fixed $(Q, J, C)$, fixed\\n$(\\\\phi, J, C)$, \
fixed $(Q,\\\\Omega, C)$, fixed $(Q, J, \\\\mu)$, and \
fixed\\n$(\\\\phi,\\\\Omega, C)$, where $Q$ is the electric charge, $J$ is \
the angular\\nmomentum, $C$ is the central charge, $\\\\phi$ is the electric \
potential conjugate\\nto charge, $\\\\Omega$ is the angular frequency \
conjugate to $J$, and finally,\\n$\\\\mu$ is the chemical potential. In the \
fixed $(Q, J, C)$, fixed $(\\\\phi, J,\\nC)$, and fixed $(Q, J, \\\\mu)$ \
ensembles, we find a topological charge of $+1$.\\nIn the fixed \
$(Q,\\\\Omega, C)$ and fixed $(\\\\phi, \\\\Omega, C)$ ensembles, \
depending\\non the values of the thermodynamic parameters, we find \
topological charges of\\n$-1$, $0$, and $+1$. Interestingly, in ensembles \
where we find the topological\\ncharge to be $0$, we observe both \
Hawking-Page and Davies type phase\\ntransitions. We show that both types of \
these phase transitions can be studied\\nusing a common vector field, and the \
topological charges associated with Davies\\ntype and Hawking-Page phase \
transitions are $-1$ and $+1$, respectively.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
