            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this study, we investigate the thermodynamic topology of \
the Kerr-Sen-Ads\nblack hole in restricted phase space. In the restricted \
phase space, a new\nparameter, central charge $C$, and its conjugate \
parameter $\\mu$ are\nintroduced, omitting the well-known $PdV$ term in the \
first law of black hole\nthermodynamics. We study the local and global \
topology of the black hole by\nconsidering the black hole solution as \
topological defects in the free energy\nlandscape. We compute the winding \
number and the total topological number at\nthe thermodynamic defects. For \
our analysis, we have considered five ensembles\nof Kerr-Sen-Ads black holes \
in restricted phase space: fixed $(Q, J, C)$, fixed\n$(\\phi, J, C)$, fixed \
$(Q,\\Omega, C)$, fixed $(Q, J, \\mu)$, and fixed\n$(\\phi,\\Omega, C)$, \
where $Q$ is the electric charge, $J$ is the angular\nmomentum, $C$ is the \
central charge, $\\phi$ is the electric potential conjugate\nto charge, \
$\\Omega$ is the angular frequency conjugate to $J$, and finally,\n$\\mu$ is \
the chemical potential. In the fixed $(Q, J, C)$, fixed $(\\phi, J,\nC)$, and \
fixed $(Q, J, \\mu)$ ensembles, we find a topological charge of $+1$.\nIn the \
fixed $(Q,\\Omega, C)$ and fixed $(\\phi, \\Omega, C)$ ensembles, depending\n\
on the values of the thermodynamic parameters, we find topological charges of\
\n$-1$, $0$, and $+1$. Interestingly, in ensembles where we find the \
topological\ncharge to be $0$, we observe both Hawking-Page and Davies type \
phase\ntransitions. We show that both types of these phase transitions can be \
studied\nusing a common vector field, and the topological charges associated \
with Davies\ntype and Hawking-Page phase transitions are $-1$ and $+1$, \
respectively.\n", 
