                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Quadratic quasi-normal modes, generated at second order \
in black hole\\nperturbation theory, are a promising target for testing \
gravity in the\\nnonlinear regime with next-generation gravitational wave \
detectors. While their\\nfrequencies have long been known, their amplitudes \
remain poorly studied. We\\nintroduce regular variables and compute \
amplitudes for Schwarzschild black\\nholes with the Leaver algorithm. We find \
a nonlinear ratio\\n$\\\\mathcal{R}\\\\simeq0.154e^{-0.068i}$ for the most \
excited $\\\\ell=4$ mode,\\nmatching results from Numerical Relativity. We \
also predict new low-frequency\\n$\\\\ell=2$ quadratic modes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
