           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.13442\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Brevi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lorenzo Brevi, Antonio Mandarino, and Enrico Prati\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Addressing the Non-perturbative Regime of the Quantum \
Anharmonic\\n  Oscillator by Physics-Informed Neural Networks\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, 10 figures. Comments are welcome\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"quant-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The use of deep learning in physical sciences has \
recently boosted the\\nability of researchers to tackle physical systems \
where little or no analytical\\ninsight is available. Recently, the \
Physics-Informed Neural Networks (PINNs)\\nhave been introduced as one of the \
most promising tools to solve systems of\\ndifferential equations guided by \
some physically grounded constraints. In the\\nquantum realm, such approach \
paves the way to a novel approach to solve the\\nSchroedinger equation for \
non-integrable systems. By following an unsupervised\\nlearning approach, we \
apply the PINNs to the anharmonic oscillator in which an\\ninteraction term \
proportional to the fourth power of the position coordinate is\\npresent. We \
compute the eigenenergies and the corresponding eigenfunctions\\nwhile \
varying the weight of the quartic interaction. We bridge our solutions \
to\\nthe regime where both the perturbative and the strong coupling theory \
work,\\nincluding the pure quartic oscillator. We investigate systems with \
real and\\nimaginary frequency, laying the foundation for novel numerical \
methods to\\ntackle problems emerging in quantum field theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
