            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.15219\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Piyabut Burikham\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"David Senjaya, Piyabut Burikham, Tiberiu Harko\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Exact Relativistic Scalar Quasibound States of The \
Dyonic Kerr-Sen\\n  Black Hole: Quantized Energy, and Hawking \
Radiation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"18 pages, 9 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider Klein-Gordon equation in the Dyonic \
Kerr-Sen black hole\\nbackground, which is the charged rotating axially \
symmetric solution of the\\nEinstein-Maxwell-Dilaton-Axion theory of gravity. \
The black hole incorporates\\nelectric, magnetic, dilatonic and axionic \
charges and is constructed in 3+1\\ndimensional spacetime. We begin our \
investigations with the construction of the\\nscalar field's governing \
equation, i.e., the covariant Klein-Gordon equation.\\nWith the help of the \
ansatz of separation of variables, we successfully\\nseparate the polar part, \
and find the exact solution in terms of Spheroidal\\nHarmonics, while the \
radial exact solution is obtained in terms of the\\nConfluent Heun function. \
The quantization of the quasibound state is done by\\napplying the polynomial \
condition of the Confluent Heun function that gives\\nrise to discrete \
complex-valued energy levels for massive scalar fields. The\\nreal part is \
the scalar field relativistic quantized energy, while the\\nimaginary part \
represents the quasibound states's decay. We present all of the\\nsixteen \
possible exact energy solutions for both massive and massless scalars.\\nWe \
also present the investigation the Hawking radiation of the Dyonic \
Kerr-Sen\\nblack hole's apparent horizon, via the Sigurd-Sannan method by \
making use of\\nthe obtained exact scalar wave functions. The radiation \
distribution function,\\nand the Hawking temperature are successfully \
obtained.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 24 May 2024 05:18:42 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 10 Aug 2024 14:53:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
