            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2406.08159\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jibril Ben Achour\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jibril Ben Achour and Hugo Roussille\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quadratic perturbations of the Schwarzschild black hole: \
The\\n  algebraically special sector\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"17+8 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate quadratic algebraically special \
perturbations (ASPs) of the\\nSchwarzschild black hole. Their dynamics are \
derived from the expansion up to\\nsecond order in perturbation of the most \
general algebraically special twisting\\nvacuum solution of general \
relativity. Following this strategy, we present\\nanalytical expressions for \
the axial-axial, polar-polar and polar-axial source\\nterms entering in the \
dynamical equations. We show that these complicated\\ninhomogeneous equations \
can be solved analytically and we present explicit\\nexpressions for the \
profiles of the quadratic ASPs. As expected, they exhibit\\nexponential \
growth both at the past and future horizons even in the non-linear\\nregime. \
We further use this result to analyze the quadratic zero modes and\\ntheir \
interpretation in terms of quadratic corrections to mass and spin of \
the\\nSchwarzschild black hole. The present work provides a direct extension \
beyond\\nthe linear regime of the original work by Couch and \
Newman.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
