            "authors" -> "Jibril Ben Achour and Hugo Roussille", "title" -> 
            "Quadratic perturbations of the Schwarzschild black hole: The\n  \
algebraically special sector", "comments" -> "17+8 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate quadratic algebraically special perturbations \
(ASPs) of the\nSchwarzschild black hole. Their dynamics are derived from the \
expansion up to\nsecond order in perturbation of the most general \
algebraically special twisting\nvacuum solution of general relativity. \
Following this strategy, we present\nanalytical expressions for the \
axial-axial, polar-polar and polar-axial source\nterms entering in the \
dynamical equations. We show that these complicated\ninhomogeneous equations \
can be solved analytically and we present explicit\nexpressions for the \
profiles of the quadratic ASPs. As expected, they exhibit\nexponential growth \
both at the past and future horizons even in the non-linear\nregime. We \
further use this result to analyze the quadratic zero modes and\ntheir \
interpretation in terms of quadratic corrections to mass and spin of the\n\
Schwarzschild black hole. The present work provides a direct extension beyond\
\nthe linear regime of the original work by Couch and Newman.\n", 
