               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2406.10879\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Suchetan Das\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Suchetan Das\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Stretched Horizon from Conformal Field Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages, one appendix\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, it has been observed that the Hartle-Hawking \
correlators, a\\nsignature of smooth horizon, can emerge from certain heavy \
excited state\\ncorrelators in the (manifestly non-smooth) BTZ stretched \
horizon background, in\\nthe limit when the stretched horizon approaches the \
real horizon. In this note,\\nwe develop a framework of quantizing the CFT \
modular Hamiltonian, that explains\\nthe necessity of introducing a stretched \
horizon and the emergence of thermal\\nfeatures in the AdS-Rindler and \
(planar) BTZ backgrounds. In more detail, we\\nquantize vacuum modular \
Hamiltonian on a spatial segment of $S^{1}$. Unlike\\nradial quantization, \
(Euclidean) time circles emerge naturally here which can\\nbe contracted \
smoothly to the `fixed points'(end points of the interval) of\\nthis \
quantization thus providing a direct link to thermal physics. To define \
a\\nHilbert space with discrete normalizable states and to construct a \
Virasoro\\nalgebra with finite central extension, a natural regulator \
($\\\\epsilon$) is\\nneeded around the fixed points. Eventually, in the dual \
description the fixed\\npoints correspond to the horizons of AdS-Rindler \
patch or (planar) BTZ and the\\ncut-off being the stretched horizon. We \
construct a (Lorentzian) highest weight\\nrepresentation of that Virasoro \
algebra. We further demonstrate that two point\\nfunction in a (vacuum) \
descendant state of the regulated Hilbert space will\\nreproduce thermal \
answer in $\\\\epsilon \\\\rightarrow 0$ limit which is analogous\\nto the \
recent observation of emergent thermality in stretched horizon\\nbackground. \
We also argue the thermal entropy of this quantization coincides\\nwith \
entanglement entropy of the subregion. Conversely, the \
microcanonical\\nentropy corresponding to high energy density of states \
exactly reproduce the\\nBTZ entropy. Quite remarkably, all these dominant \
high lying microstates are\\ndefined only at finite $\\\\epsilon$ in the \
regulated Hilbert space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 16 Jun 2024 10:02:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
