            "  We study timelike and conventional entanglement entropy as \
potential probes\nof black hole singularities via the AdS/CFT correspondence. \
Using an\nanalytically tractable example, we find characteristic behavior of \
holographic\ntimelike entanglement entropy when the geometry involves a \
curvature\nsingularity. We also observe interesting phenomena that, in some \
particular\nsetups, holographic timelike and conventional entanglement \
entropy are\ndetermined from multiple complex saddle points, which fall \
outside the\nassumptions of the Lewkowycz-Maldacena type argument.\n", 
