                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  General Relativity predicts the existence of quadratic \
quasi-normal modes at\\nsecond order in perturbation theory. Building on our \
recent work, we compute\\nthe amplitudes and polarizations of these modes for \
non-rotating black holes,\\nshowing that they are completely determined by \
the amplitudes and polarizations\\nof linear modes. We obtain the ratio of \
quadratic to linear amplitudes, which\\nstill depends on the initial \
conditions of the merger through the polarization\\nof linear modes. However, \
we demonstrate that this dependence is captured by\\nfour fundamental \
numbers, independent of initial conditions, representing four\\ndifferent \
combinations of linear modes parities. Additionally, we prove two\\nselection \
rules regarding the vanishing of classes of quadratic modes. Our\\nresults \
are available online as a package which provides the ratio of\\namplitudes \
across a broad spectrum of angular momenta.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
