            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2406.17205\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Allic Sivaramakrishnan\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Allic Sivaramakrishnan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Correlators of Worldline Proper Length\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"45 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el gr-qc hep-ph quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A classical observer can measure elapsed proper time \
along their worldline.\\nWhen observers are coupled to a system with internal \
correlations, measurements\\nof elapsed time may inherit these correlations. \
We show that derivatives of the\\non-shell action with respect to worldline \
mass compute correlation functions of\\nworldline proper length at tree \
level. We study worldlines coupled to a scalar\\nfield. We calculate the \
length-length two-point function and find it arises\\nfrom correlated path \
fluctuations. As an application, we propose that the\\nlogarithm of local \
correlators serves as a generating function of length\\ncorrelators, which \
generalizes the on-shell action prescription. Using this\\nproposal, we \
extract AdS worldline observables from local CFT correlators as\\ncomputed by \
Witten diagrams. We briefly discuss extensions to gravity,\\ninterferometers, \
and the holographic encoding of observer time.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
