 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Thermal spectra of correlation functions in holographic \
3d large-N CFTs\\ncorrespond to quasinormal modes of classical gravity and \
other fields in\\nasymptotically anti-de Sitter black hole spacetimes. Using \
general properties\\nof such spectra along with constraints imposed by the \
S-duality (or the\\nparticle-vortex duality), we derive a spectral duality \
relation that all such\\nspectra must obey. Its form is universal in that \
each such relation (expressed\\nas an infinite product over QNMs) only \
depends on a single function of a\\nspatial wavevector that corresponds to \
the bulk algebraically special\\nfrequencies. In the process, we also derive \
a new sum rule constraining\\nproducts over QNMs. The spectral duality \
relation, which imposes an infinite\\nset of constraints on the QNMs, is then \
investigated and a number of well-known\\nholographic examples that \
demonstrate its validity are examined. Our results\\nalso allow us to \
understand several new aspects of the pole-skipping\\nphenomenon.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
