                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review constructions of three-dimensional `quantum' \
black holes. Such\\nspacetimes arise via holographic braneworlds and are \
exact solutions to an\\ninduced higher-derivative theory of gravity \
consistently coupled to a large$-c$\\nquantum field theory with an \
ultraviolet cutoff, accounting for all orders of\\nsemi-classical \
backreaction. Notably, such quantum-corrected black holes are\\nmuch larger \
than the Planck length. We describe the geometry and horizon\\nthermodynamics \
of a host of asymptotically (anti-) de Sitter and flat quantum\\nblack holes. \
A summary of higher-dimensional extensions is given. We survey\\nmultiple \
applications of quantum black holes and braneworld holography.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
