               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2407.04128\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Carlo Heissenberg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Francesco Alessio, Paolo Di Vecchia, Carlo \
Heissenberg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Logarithmic soft theorems and soft spectra\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"41 pages + references. V2: Presentation expanded and \
improved. We\\n  include several new results based on the resummed waveform \
that captures all\\n  leading logarithms for a background $2\\\\to2$ hard \
process\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using universal predictions provided by classical soft \
theorems, we revisit\\nthe energy emission spectrum for gravitational \
scatterings of compact objects\\nin the low-frequency expansion. We calculate \
this observable beyond the\\nzero-frequency limit, retaining an exact \
dependence on the kinematics of the\\nmassive objects. This allows us to \
study independently the ultrarelativistic or\\nmassless limit, where we find \
agreement with the literature, and the\\nsmall-deflection or post-Minkowskian \
(PM) limit, where we provide explicit\\nresults up to $\\\\mathcal{O}(G^5)$. \
These confirm that the high-velocity limit of\\na given PM order is smoothly \
connected to the corresponding massless result\\nwhenever the latter is \
analytic in the Newton constant $G$. We also provide\\nexplicit expressions \
for the waveforms to order $\\\\omega^{-1}$, \
$\\\\log\\\\omega$,\\n$\\\\omega(\\\\log\\\\omega)^2$ in the soft limit, \
$\\\\omega\\\\to0$, expanded up to\\nsub-subleading PM order, as well as a \
conjecture for the logarithmic soft terms\\nof the type \
$\\\\omega^{n-1}(\\\\log\\\\omega)^{n}$ with $n\\\\ge 3$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
