         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2407.04128", "submitter" -> "Carlo Heissenberg", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Francesco Alessio, Paolo Di Vecchia, Carlo Heissenberg", "title" -> 
            "Logarithmic soft theorems and soft spectra", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages + references. V2: Presentation expanded and improved. \
We\n  include several new results based on the resummed waveform that \
captures all\n  leading logarithms for a background $2\\to2$ hard process", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Using universal predictions provided by classical soft \
theorems, we revisit\nthe energy emission spectrum for gravitational \
scatterings of compact objects\nin the low-frequency expansion. We calculate \
this observable beyond the\nzero-frequency limit, retaining an exact \
dependence on the kinematics of the\nmassive objects. This allows us to study \
independently the ultrarelativistic or\nmassless limit, where we find \
agreement with the literature, and the\nsmall-deflection or post-Minkowskian \
(PM) limit, where we provide explicit\nresults up to $\\mathcal{O}(G^5)$. \
These confirm that the high-velocity limit of\na given PM order is smoothly \
connected to the corresponding massless result\nwhenever the latter is \
analytic in the Newton constant $G$. We also provide\nexplicit expressions \
for the waveforms to order $\\omega^{-1}$, $\\log\\omega$,\n\
$\\omega(\\log\\omega)^2$ in the soft limit, $\\omega\\to0$, expanded up to\n\
sub-subleading PM order, as well as a conjecture for the logarithmic soft \
terms\nof the type $\\omega^{n-1}(\\log\\omega)^{n}$ with $n\\ge 3$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 4 Jul 2024 19:05:04 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 13 Sep 2024 15:12:36 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-09-16", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Alessio", "Francesco", ""}, {
              "Di Vecchia", "Paolo", ""}, {"Heissenberg", "Carlo", ""}}}], 
