                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Differential equations are powerful tools in the study \
of correlation\\nfunctions in conformal field theories (CFTs). Carrollian \
amplitudes behave as\\ncorrelation functions of Carrollian CFT that \
holographically describes\\nasymptotically flat spacetime. We derive linear \
differential equations\\nsatisfied by Carrollian MHV gluon and graviton \
amplitudes. We obtain\\nnon-distributional solutions for both the gluon and \
graviton cases. We perform\\nvarious consistency checks for these \
differential equations, including\\ncompatibility with conformal Carrollian \
symmetries.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
