           "id" -> "2407.06009", "submitter" -> "Lodovico Capuano", "authors" -> 
            "Lodovico Capuano, Luca Santoni, Enrico Barausse", "title" -> 
            "Perturbations of the Vaidya metric in the frequency domain: \
Quasi-normal\n  modes and tidal response", "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The mass of a black hole can dynamically evolve due to various \
physical\nprocesses, such as for instance accretion, Hawking radiation, \
absorption of\ngravitational/electromagnetic waves, superradiance, etc. This \
evolution can\nhave an impact on astrophysical observables, like the ringdown \
gravitational\nsignal. An effective description of a spherically symmetric \
black hole with\nevolving mass is provided by the Vaidya metric. In our \
investigation, we\nexplore the dynamics of linear perturbations on this \
background, assuming a\nconstant rate of change for the mass. Despite the \
time-dependent background, a\njudicious change of coordinates allows us to \
treat the perturbations in the\nfrequency domain, and to compute explicitly \
the quasi-normal modes and the\ntidal Love numbers.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
