, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We discuss the dynamics of a (neutral) test particle \
in Topological Star\\nspacetime undergoing scattering processes by a \
superposed test radiation field,\\na situation that in a 4D black hole \
spacetime is known as relativistic\\nPoynting-Robertson effect, paving the \
way for future studies involving\\nradiation-reaction effects. Furthermore, \
we study self-force-driven evolution\\nof a scalar field, perturbing the \
Top-Star spacetime with a scalar charge\\ncurrent. The latter for simplicity \
is taken to be circular, equatorial and\\ngeodetic. To perform this study, \
besides solving all the self-force related\\nproblem (regularization of all \
divergences due to the self-field, mode sum\\nregularization, etc.), we had \
to adapt the 4D Mano-Suzuki-Takasugi formalism to\\nthe present 5D situation. \
Finally, we have compared this formalism with the\\n(quantum) Seiberg-Witten \
formalism, both related to the solutions of a Heun\\nConfluent Equation, but \
appearing in different contexts in the literature,\\nblack hole perturbation \
theory the first, quantum curves in super-Yang-Mills\\ntheories the \
second.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
