            "  We propose a scenario of primordial gravitational atoms \
(PGAs), which may\nexist in the current and past universe due to spinning \
primordial black holes\n(PBHs) and very light bosonic fields. In a \
monochromatic mass scenario with a\nsizable dimensionless spin, which may \
arise in a short matter dominated (MD)\nera, we analyze the resulting \
stochastic gravitational wave background (SGWB)\nsignal. Its spectrum is \
approximately characterized by a rising $\\propto f^3$\nfollowed by a falling \
$\\propto f^{-1}$ where $f$ is the frequency. Then, we\ninvestigate the \
constraints and prospects of such a SGWB, and find that PGAs\nwith a core \
mass $M_{\\rm BH}\\sim {\\cal O}(10)~M_{\\odot}$ and a cloud of light\nscalar \
with mass $\\mu \\sim {\\cal O} (10^{-13})$ eV could yield constraints even\n\
stronger than those from bare PBHs. Future detectors such as LISA, Taiji and\n\
TianQin are able to explore PGAs over a narrow and elongated strap in the\n$(\
\\mu,M_{\\rm BH})$ plane, spanning over 10 orders of magnitude for the \
maximum\nspin, $10^{-8}~M_{\\odot}\\lesssim M_{\\rm BH}\\lesssim \
10^4~M_{\\odot}$,\n$10^{-16}~{\\rm eV}\\lesssim \\mu\\lesssim 10^{-3}~\\rm \
eV$. If the PGA is dressed\nwith a vector cloud, the SGWB signal has a much \
better opportunity to be\nprobed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 18 Jul 2024 10:43:32 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-07-22", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kang", "Zhaofeng", ""}, {
              "Li", "Tianjun", ""}, {"Ye", "Weitao", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
