                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Julien Barrat, Bartomeu Fiol, Enrico Marchetto, Alessio \
Miscioscia and\\n  Elli Pomoni\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Conformal line defects at finite temperature\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"38 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DESY-24-099\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study conformal field theories at finite \
temperature in the presence of a\\ntemporal conformal line defect, wrapping \
the thermal circle, akin to a Polyakov\\nloop in gauge theories. Although \
several symmetries of the conformal group are\\nbroken, the model can still \
be highly constrained from its features at\\nzero-temperature. In this work \
we show that the defect and bulk one and\\ntwo-point correlators can be \
written as functions of zero-temperature data and\\nthermal one-point \
functions (defect and bulk). The defect one-point functions\\nare new data \
and they are induced by thermal effects of the bulk. For this new\\nset of \
data we derive novel sum rules and establish a bootstrap problem for \
the\\nthermal defect one-point functions from the KMS condition. We also \
comment on\\nthe behaviour of operators with large scaling dimensions. \
Additionally, we\\nrelate the free energy and entropy density to the OPE data \
through the\\none-point function of the stress-energy tensor. Our formalism \
is validated\\nthrough analytical computations in generalized free scalar \
field theory, and we\\npresent new predictions for the O(N) model with a \
magnetic impurity in the\\n$\\\\varepsilon$-expansion and the large N \
limit.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
