Miscioscia and\n  Elli Pomoni", "title" -> 
             "Conformal line defects at finite temperature", "comments" -> 
             "38 pages, 2 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
             "report-no" -> "DESY-24-099", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study conformal field theories at finite temperature in \
the presence of a\ntemporal conformal line defect, wrapping the thermal \
circle, akin to a Polyakov\nloop in gauge theories. Although several \
symmetries of the conformal group are\nbroken, the model can still be highly \
constrained from its features at\nzero-temperature. In this work we show that \
the defect and bulk one and\ntwo-point correlators can be written as \
functions of zero-temperature data and\nthermal one-point functions (defect \
and bulk). The defect one-point functions\nare new data and they are induced \
by thermal effects of the bulk. For this new\nset of data we derive novel sum \
rules and establish a bootstrap problem for the\nthermal defect one-point \
functions from the KMS condition. We also comment on\nthe behaviour of \
operators with large scaling dimensions. Additionally, we\nrelate the free \
energy and entropy density to the OPE data through the\none-point function of \
the stress-energy tensor. Our formalism is validated\nthrough analytical \
computations in generalized free scalar field theory, and we\npresent new \
predictions for the O(N) model with a magnetic impurity in the\n\
$\\varepsilon$-expansion and the large N limit.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
