               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2407.19654\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Chao Zhang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chao Zhang and Anzhong Wang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quasi-Normal Modes of Loop Quantum Black Holes Formed \
from Gravitational\\n  Collapse\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper, we study the quasi-normal modes (QNMs) \
of a scalar field in\\nthe background of a large class of quantum black holes \
that can be formed from\\ngravitational collapse of a dust fluid in the \
framework of effective loop\\nquantum gravity. The loop quantum black holes \
(LQBHs) are characterized by\\nthree free parameters, one of which is the \
mass parameter, while the other two\\nare purely due to quantum geometric \
effects. Among these two quantum\\nparameters, one is completely fixed by \
black hole thermodynamics and its\\neffects are negligible for macroscopic \
black holes, while the second parameter\\nis completely free (in principle). \
In the studies of the QNMs of such LQBHs, we\\npay particular attention to \
the difference of the QNMs between LQBHs and\\nclassical ones, so that they \
can be observed for the current and forthcoming\\ngravitational wave \
observations, whereby place the LQBH theory directly under\\nthe test of \
observations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
