            "Chao Zhang and Anzhong Wang", "title" -> 
            
            "Quasi-Normal Modes of Loop Quantum Black Holes Formed from \
Gravitational\n  Collapse", "comments" -> "10 pages, 3 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper, we study the quasi-normal modes (QNMs) of a \
scalar field in\nthe background of a large class of quantum black holes that \
can be formed from\ngravitational collapse of a dust fluid in the framework \
of effective loop\nquantum gravity. The loop quantum black holes (LQBHs) are \
characterized by\nthree free parameters, one of which is the mass parameter, \
while the other two\nare purely due to quantum geometric effects. Among these \
two quantum\nparameters, one is completely fixed by black hole thermodynamics \
and its\neffects are negligible for macroscopic black holes, while the second \
parameter\nis completely free (in principle). In the studies of the QNMs of \
such LQBHs, we\npay particular attention to the difference of the QNMs \
between LQBHs and\nclassical ones, so that they can be observed for the \
current and forthcoming\ngravitational wave observations, whereby place the \
LQBH theory directly under\nthe test of observations.\n", 
