 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We employ the isomonodromic method to study linear \
scalar massive\\nperturbations of Kerr black holes for generic scalar masses \
$M\\\\mu$ and generic\\nblack hole spins $a/M$. A degeneracy between the \
longest-living quasinormal\\nmode and the first overtone is found for \
$(M\\\\mu)_c \\\\simeq 0.3704981$ and\\n$(a/M)_c\\\\simeq 0.9994660$. We show \
that the longest-living mode and the first\\novertone change continuously \
into each other as we vary the parameters around\\nthe point of degeneracy, \
providing evidence for the existence of a geometric\\nphase around an \
exceptional point. We interpret our findings through a\\nthermodynamic \
analogy.\\n\""}]}, {
