            "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper studies AdS/CFT in its $p$-adic version (at the \
``finite place\")\nin the setting where the bulk geometry is made up of the \
Tate curve, a discrete\nquotient of the Bruhat-Tits tree. Generalizing a \
classic result due to\nZabrodin, the boundary dual of the free massive bulk \
theory is explicitly\nderived. Introducing perturbative interactions, the \
Wittens diagrams for the\ntwo-point and three-point correlators are computed \
for generic scaling\ndimensions at one-loop and tree level respectively. The \
answers obtained\ndemonstrate how $p$-adic AdS/CFT on the Tate curve provides \
a useful toy model\nfor real CFTs at finite temperature.\n", 
