               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2408.05790\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthew Dodelson\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthew Dodelson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ringdown in the SYK model\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-TH-2024-135\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze thermal correlators in the Sachdev-Ye-Kitaev \
model away from the\\nmaximally chaotic limit. Despite the absence of a \
weakly curved black hole\\ndual, the two point function decomposes into a sum \
over a discrete set of\\nquasinormal modes. To compute the spectrum of modes, \
we analytically solve the\\nSchwinger-Dyson equations to a high order in \
perturbation theory, and then\\nnumerically fit to a sum of exponentials \
using a technique analogous to the\\ndouble cone construction. The resulting \
spectrum has a tree-like structure\\nwhich is reminiscent of AdS black holes \
with curvature singularities. We\\npresent a simple toy model of stringy \
black holes that qualitatively reproduces\\nsome aspects of this \
structure.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
