               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Piyabut Burikham\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Teephatai Bunyaratavej, Piyabut Burikham, David \
Senjaya\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Revisiting Chronology Protection Conjecture in The Dyonic \
Kerr-Sen Black\\n  Hole Spacetime\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 pages, 11 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Chronology Protection Conjecture (CPC) was first \
introduced by Hawking\\nafter his semi-classical investigation to the \
behaviour of a spacetime with\\nclosed timelike curves (CTCs) in response to \
scalar perturbation. It is argued\\nthat there would be instabilities leading \
to amplification of the perturbation\\nand finally causing collapse of the \
region with CTCs. In this work, we\\ninvestigate the CPC by exactly solve the \
Klein-Gordon equation in the region\\ninside the inner horizon of the \
non-extremal Dyonic Kerr-Sen~(KS) black hole,\\nwhere closed timelike curves \
exist. Successfully find the exact radial\\nsolution, we apply the polynomial \
condition that turns into rule of the energy\\nquantization. The quasinormal \
modes~(QNMs) of the scalar fields in the region\\ninside the inner horizon of \
the rotating black hole with nonzero energy have\\nonly positive imaginary \
part describing states that grow in time. The\\nexponentially growing modes \
will backreact and deform the spacetime region\\nwhere CTC exists. The CPC is \
proven to be valid in the Dyonic Kerr-Sen black\\nhole spacetime. Moreover, \
since the Dyonic Kerr-Sen black hole is the most\\ngeneral axisymmetric black \
hole solution of the string inspired\\nEinstein-Maxwell-dilaton-axion (EMDA) \
theory, the semiclassical proof in this\\nwork is also valid for all simpler \
rotating black holes of the EMDA theory. The\\nstructure of the Dyonic KS \
spacetime distinctive from the Kerr-Newman\\ncounterpart is also explored.\\n\
\""}]}, {
