, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this paper, we evaluate the one loop partition \
function of a scalar field\\nin the near horizon geometry of the extremal \
Reissner Nordstr\\\\\\\"{o}m black hole\\nfrom an infinite product over \
quasinormal modes using the\\nDenef-Hartnoll-Sachdev (DHS) formula. We show \
that, the logarithmic divergent\\nterm of the one loop partition function \
computed using the DHS formula agrees\\nwith the heat kernel method. Using \
the same formula, we also evaluate the one\\nloop partition function of \
scalar field in the near extremal Kerr Newman black\\nhole and observe that \
it reduces to the same in the near horizon $AdS_2\\\\times\\nS^2$ geometry of \
the extremal Reissner Nordstr\\\\\\\"{o}m black hole when the\\nangular \
velocity at the horizon is tuned to $2\\\\pi T_{BH}$ value. We \
observe\\nthat, for higher spin fields, the mode functions become irregular \
at the\\nhorizon for certain quasinormal frequencies and therefore we remove \
them to\\nobtain the one loop determinant.\\n\""}]}, {
