               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gravitational Wave Tails from Soft Theorem: A Short \
Review\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LaTeX; 25 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th astro-ph.CO gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  If a set of massive objects collide in space and the \
fragments disperse,\\npossibly forming black holes, then this process will \
emit gravitational waves.\\nComputing the detailed gravitational wave-form \
associated with this process is\\na complicated problem, not only due to the \
non-linearity of gravity but also\\ndue to the fact that during the collision \
and subsequent fragmentation the\\nobjects could undergo complicated \
non-gravitational interactions. Nevertheless\\nthe classical soft graviton \
theorem determines the power law fall-off of the\\nwave-form at late and \
early times, including logarithmic corrections, in terms\\nof only the \
momenta of the incoming and outgoing objects without any reference\\nto what \
transpired during the collision. In this short review I shall explain\\nthe \
results and very briefly outline the derivation of these results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 16 Aug 2024 17:22:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-08-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sen\"", ",", "\"Ashoke\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
