             "Jo\\~ao Paulo Cavalcante, Maur\\'icio Richartz and Bruno \
Carneiro da\n  Cunha", "title" -> 
             "Massive scalar perturbations in Kerr Black Holes: near extremal \
analysis", "comments" -> "20 pages, 13 graphics, 2 figures, 2 tables", 
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study quasinormal modes of massive scalar perturbations in \
Kerr black\nholes using the isomonodromic method. For arbitrary scalar masses \
$M \\mu$ and\nblack hole spins $a/M$, we numerically determine the \
quasinormal frequencies\nfor various orbital $\\ell$, azimuthal $m$, and \
overtone $n$ numbers. In\nparticular, we derive an analytic expression for \
frequencies of the\nzero-damping modes near the extremal limit $a/M \
\\rightarrow 1$. For $\\ell=m=1$,\nwe reveal that the fundamental mode \
becomes a damped mode (rather than a\nzero-damping mode) if the scalar field \
is sufficiently heavy. By exploring the\nparameter space, we find numerical \
evidence for level-crossing between the\nlongest-living mode and the first \
overtone at an exceptional point $(M\\mu)_c\n\\simeq 0.3704981$ and \
$(a/M)_c\\simeq 0.9994660$.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
