                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alexander Tyukov\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"David Turton, Alexander Tyukov\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Four-point correlators in N=4 SYM from AdS$_5$ bubbling \
geometries\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"26 pages\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Four-point correlation functions are observables of \
significant interest in\\nholographic field theories. We compute an infinite \
family of four-point\\ncorrelation functions of operators in short multiplets \
of 4D N=4 super\\nYang-Mills theory in the supergravity regime, by studying \
the quadratic\\nfluctuations around non-trivial supergravity backgrounds. The \
supergravity\\nbackgrounds are supersymmetric smooth geometries in the family \
derived by Lin,\\nLunin and Maldacena. The light probes comprise an infinite \
sequence of\\nKaluza-Klein harmonics of the dilaton/axion. For generic \
parameter values, the\\nsupergravity backgrounds are dual to heavy CFT \
states. However we focus on the\\nlimit in which the dual CFT states become \
light single-particle states. The\\nresulting all-light four-point \
correlators are related by superconformal Ward\\nidentities to previously \
known four-point correlators of half-BPS chiral\\nprimary operators. By \
verifying that the Ward identities are satisfied, we\\nconfirm the validity \
of the supergravity method.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 29 Aug 2024 18:00:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-09-02\""}]}, {
