             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Four-point correlation functions are observables of \
significant interest in\nholographic field theories. We compute an infinite \
family of four-point\ncorrelation functions of operators in short multiplets \
of 4D N=4 super\nYang-Mills theory in the supergravity regime, by studying \
the quadratic\nfluctuations around non-trivial supergravity backgrounds. The \
supergravity\nbackgrounds are supersymmetric smooth geometries in the family \
derived by Lin,\nLunin and Maldacena. The light probes comprise an infinite \
sequence of\nKaluza-Klein harmonics of the dilaton/axion. For generic \
parameter values, the\nsupergravity backgrounds are dual to heavy CFT states. \
However we focus on the\nlimit in which the dual CFT states become light \
single-particle states. The\nresulting all-light four-point correlators are \
related by superconformal Ward\nidentities to previously known four-point \
correlators of half-BPS chiral\nprimary operators. By verifying that the Ward \
identities are satisfied, we\nconfirm the validity of the supergravity \
method.\n", "versions" -> {{
