             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2409.05519\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Baishali Roy\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Suman Das, Somnath Porey, Baishali Roy\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Brick Wall in AdS-Schwarzschild Black Hole: Normal Modes \
and Emerging\\n  Thermality\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"34 pages, 22 figures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  This paper investigates the normal modes of a probe \
scalar field in a\\nfive-dimensional AdS-Schwarzschild black hole with the \
brick wall boundary\\ncondition near the horizon. We employ various \
techniques to compute the\\nspectrum and analyze its properties. Our results \
reveal a linear dependence of\\nthe spectrum on the principal quantum number \
while demonstrating a non-trivial\\ndependence on the angular momentum \
quantum number. We compute the Spectral Form\\nFactor (SFF) and find a \
dip-ramp-plateau structure, with the slope of the ramp\\napproaching unity as \
the brick wall nears the horizon. We also observe that as\\nthe brick wall \
approaches the horizon, the poles of the retarded Green's\\nfunction condense \
on the real line, leading to an emergent thermal behavior in\\nthe boundary \
theory. This work extends previous studies on lower-dimensional\\nblack holes \
to higher dimensions, providing insights into the connection\\nbetween black \
hole microstate models and boundary chaos. Our findings\\ncontribute to the \
ongoing discussions on the information paradox and the nature\\nof black hole \
interiors in the context of AdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Sep 2024 11:25:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
