          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "2409.11666", "submitter" -> "Di Wu", "authors" -> 
             "Wentao Liu, Li Zhang, Di Wu, Jieci Wang", "title" -> 
             "Thermodynamic topological classes of the rotating, accelerating \
black\n  holes", "comments" -> "28 pages, 9 figures, 1 table, JHEP3.cls", 
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  In this paper, we extend our previous work [D. Wu, Phys. Rev. \
D 108, 084041\n(2023)] to more general cases by including a rotation \
parameter. We investigate\nthe topological numbers for the rotating, \
accelerating neutral black hole and\nits AdS extension, as well as the \
rotating, accelerating charged black hole and\nits AdS extension. We find \
that the topological number of an asymptotically\nflat accelerating black \
hole consistently differs by one from that of its\nnon-accelerating \
counterpart. Furthermore, we show that for an asymptotically\nAdS \
accelerating black hole, the topological number is reduced by one compared\n\
to its non-accelerating AdS counterpart. In addition, we demonstrate that\n\
within the framework of general relativity, the acceleration parameter and \
the\nnegative cosmological constant each independently add one to the \
topological\nnumber. However, when both factors are present, their effects \
neutralize each\nother, resulting in no overall change to the topological \
number.\n", "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 18 Sep 2024 03:03:10 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2024-09-19", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Liu", "Wentao", ""}, {
               "Zhang", "Li", ""}, {"Wu", "Di", ""}, {"Wang", "Jieci", ""}}}],
            "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{7.306704670043855, 1.2534117921705366`}, 
           0.08283829248930569],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2409.12747\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Di Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Xiao-Dan Zhu, Wentao Liu, Di Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Universal thermodynamic topological classes of rotating \
black holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"11 pages, 8 figures, 4 tables, revtex4-1.cls. Submitted \
to PRD on\\n  September 19th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In a recent study, Wei et al. [arXiv:2409.09333] \
proposed a universal\\nclassification scheme that interprets black hole \
solutions as topological\\ndefects within the thermodynamic parameter space, \
and then divides black hole\\nsolutions into four distinct classes, denoted \
as $W^{1-}$, $W^{0+}$, $W^{0-}$,\\nand $W^{1+}$, offering insights into \
deeper aspects of black hole\\nthermodynamics and gravity. In this paper, we \
investigate the universal\\nthermodynamic topological classification of the \
singly rotating Kerr black\\nholes in all dimensions, as well as the \
four-dimensional Kerr-Newman black\\nhole. We show that the innermost small \
black hole states of the $d \\\\geq 6$\\nsingly rotating Kerr black holes are \
thermodynamically unstable, while those of\\nthe four-dimensional Kerr-Newman \
black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating\\nKerr black holes are \
thermodynamically stable. On the other hand, the outermost\\nlarge black \
holes exhibit unstable behavior in all these cases. At the\\nlow-temperature \
limit, the $d \\\\geq 6$ singly rotating Kerr black holes have one\\nlarge \
thermodynamically unstable black hole, while the \
four-dimensional\\nKerr-Newman black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating \
Kerr black holes\\nfeature one large unstable branch and one small stable \
branch. Conversely, at\\nthe high-temperature limit, the $d \\\\geq 6$ singly \
rotating Kerr black holes\\nexhibit a small unstable black hole state, while \
the four-dimensional\\nKerr-Newman black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly \
rotating Kerr black holes have\\nno black hole states at all. Consequently, \
we demonstrate that the $d \\\\geq 6$\\nsingly rotating Kerr black holes \
belong to the class $W^{1-}$, whereas the\\nfour-dimensional Kerr-Newman and \
$d = 4, 5$ singly rotating Kerr black holes\\nbelong to the class $W^{0+}$, \
thereby further support the conjecture proposed\\nin \
[arXiv:2409.09333].\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 19 Sep 2024 13:13:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-09-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
