          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2409.12747", "submitter" -> "Di Wu", "authors" -> 
            "Xiao-Dan Zhu, Wentao Liu, Di Wu", "title" -> 
            "Universal thermodynamic topological classes of rotating black \
holes", "comments" -> 
            "11 pages, 8 figures, 4 tables, revtex4-1.cls. Submitted to PRD \
on\n  September 19th", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In a recent study, Wei et al. [arXiv:2409.09333] proposed a \
universal\nclassification scheme that interprets black hole solutions as \
topological\ndefects within the thermodynamic parameter space, and then \
divides black hole\nsolutions into four distinct classes, denoted as \
$W^{1-}$, $W^{0+}$, $W^{0-}$,\nand $W^{1+}$, offering insights into deeper \
aspects of black hole\nthermodynamics and gravity. In this paper, we \
investigate the universal\nthermodynamic topological classification of the \
singly rotating Kerr black\nholes in all dimensions, as well as the \
four-dimensional Kerr-Newman black\nhole. We show that the innermost small \
black hole states of the $d \\geq 6$\nsingly rotating Kerr black holes are \
thermodynamically unstable, while those of\nthe four-dimensional Kerr-Newman \
black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating\nKerr black holes are \
thermodynamically stable. On the other hand, the outermost\nlarge black holes \
exhibit unstable behavior in all these cases. At the\nlow-temperature limit, \
the $d \\geq 6$ singly rotating Kerr black holes have one\nlarge \
thermodynamically unstable black hole, while the four-dimensional\n\
Kerr-Newman black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating Kerr black holes\n\
feature one large unstable branch and one small stable branch. Conversely, at\
\nthe high-temperature limit, the $d \\geq 6$ singly rotating Kerr black \
holes\nexhibit a small unstable black hole state, while the four-dimensional\n\
Kerr-Newman black hole and the $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating Kerr black holes \
have\nno black hole states at all. Consequently, we demonstrate that the $d \
\\geq 6$\nsingly rotating Kerr black holes belong to the class $W^{1-}$, \
whereas the\nfour-dimensional Kerr-Newman and $d = 4, 5$ singly rotating Kerr \
black holes\nbelong to the class $W^{0+}$, thereby further support the \
conjecture proposed\nin [arXiv:2409.09333].\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 19 Sep 2024 13:13:48 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-09-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Zhu", "Xiao-Dan", ""}, {
              "Liu", "Wentao", ""}, {"Wu", "Di", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
