           "id" -> "2409.12898", "submitter" -> "Samim Akhtar", "authors" -> 
            "Samim Akhtar", "title" -> 
            "On the classical limit of the (sub)$^{n}$-leading soft graviton \
theorems\n  in $D = 4$ without deflection", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Tree-level gravitational amplitudes satisfy an infinite \
hierarchy of soft\nfactorization theorems. The existence of these theorems \
has been recently\nlinked with the existence of an infinite tower of \
asymptotic symmetries. In\nthis paper, we analyze the relevance of the soft \
graviton theorems beyond\nsub-leading order in the context of classical \
gravitational scattering in four\ndimensions. More in detail, we show that \
the infinite impact parameter limit of\nthe late-time gravitational field \
emitted during a classical scattering can be\nderived using these \
factorization theorems. The classical field obtained in\nthis (infinite \
impact parameter) regime has an expansion in the frequency of\nthe detector \
where the modes scale as $\\omega^{n}\\log{\\omega}$ with a vanishing\n\
memory.\n", 
